1
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:18,790
Smeagol!

2
00:01:18,790 --> 00:01:21,560
I've got one!

3
00:01:21,670 --> 00:01:23,840
I've got a fish, Smeag. Smeagol!

4
00:01:23,840 --> 00:01:27,490
Pull it in. Go on. Go on. Go on. Pull it in.

5
00:01:35,180 --> 00:01:37,500
Deagol!

6
00:02:34,410 --> 00:02:36,770
Deagol?

7
00:02:38,790 --> 00:02:41,560
Deagol.

8
00:02:56,850 --> 00:02:59,420
Give us that, Deagol, my love.

9
00:03:03,900 --> 00:03:05,710
Why?

10
00:03:06,280 --> 00:03:08,700
Because...

11
00:03:08,700 --> 00:03:12,970
it's my birthday and I wants it.

12
00:04:35,700 --> 00:04:51,590
My precious  They cursed us.

13
00:04:51,590 --> 00:04:53,180
Murderer.

14
00:04:53,180 --> 00:04:55,810
"Murderer" they called us.

15
00:04:55,810 --> 00:05:01,080
They cursed us and drove us away.

16
00:05:01,730 --> 00:05:03,570
Gollum.

17
00:05:03,570 --> 00:05:05,480
Gollum.

18
00:05:05,480 --> 00:05:07,920
Gollum.

19
00:05:10,950 --> 00:05:14,160
And we wept, precious.

20
00:05:14,160 --> 00:05:18,230
We wept to be so alone.

21
00:05:20,290 --> 00:05:24,610
and cool so nice for feet

22
00:05:25,090 --> 00:05:29,630
And we only wish to catch a fish

23
00:05:29,630 --> 00:05:33,410
so juicy sweet

24
00:05:38,690 --> 00:05:42,940
And we forgot the taste of bread...

25
00:05:42,940 --> 00:05:47,090
the sound of trees...

26
00:05:47,440 --> 00:05:51,180
the softness of the wind.

27
00:05:51,280 --> 00:05:57,480
We even forgot our own name.

28
00:06:05,130 --> 00:06:12,030
My precious.

29
00:06:55,810 --> 00:06:58,540
Wake up!

30
00:06:59,060 --> 00:07:00,900
Wake up!

31
00:07:00,900 --> 00:07:02,860
Wake up, sleepies.

32
00:07:02,860 --> 00:07:04,900
We must go, yes.

33
00:07:04,900 --> 00:07:08,090
We must go at once.

34
00:07:11,160 --> 00:07:14,720
Haven't you had any sleep, Mr. Frodo?

35
00:07:16,450 --> 00:07:19,520
I've gone and had too much.

36
00:07:20,370 --> 00:07:22,290
Must be getting late.

37
00:07:22,290 --> 00:07:23,960
No.

38
00:07:23,960 --> 00:07:26,050
It isn't.

39
00:07:26,050 --> 00:07:29,220
It isn't midday yet.

40
00:07:29,220 --> 00:07:32,370
The days are growing darker.

41
00:07:36,060 --> 00:07:38,790
Come on!

42
00:07:40,730 --> 00:07:43,150
Must go! No time!

43
00:07:43,150 --> 00:07:45,690
Not before Mr. Frodo's had something to eat.

44
00:07:45,690 --> 00:07:49,090
No time to lose, silly.

45
00:07:57,330 --> 00:07:59,100
Here.

46
00:08:01,830 --> 00:08:03,790
What about you?

47
00:08:03,790 --> 00:08:07,740
no, I'm not hungry. Leastways, not for lembas bread.

48
00:08:07,760 --> 00:08:09,700
Sam.

49
00:08:11,760 --> 00:08:13,430
All right.

50
00:08:13,430 --> 00:08:16,100
We don't have that much left.

51
00:08:16,100 --> 00:08:19,540
We have to be careful or we're going to run out.

52
00:08:21,150 --> 00:08:24,270
You go ahead and eat that, Mr. Frodo.

53
00:08:24,270 --> 00:08:26,150
I've rationed it.

54
00:08:26,150 --> 00:08:28,380
There should be enough.

55
00:08:29,990 --> 00:08:31,760
For what?

56
00:08:32,910 --> 00:08:35,140
The journey home.

57
00:08:42,460 --> 00:08:45,320
Come, Hobbitses.

58
00:08:46,170 --> 00:08:48,260
Very close now.

59
00:08:48,260 --> 00:08:51,640
Very close to Mordor.

60
00:08:51,640 --> 00:08:54,470
No safe places here.

61
00:08:54,470 --> 00:08:57,160
Hurry.

62
00:09:45,650 --> 00:09:49,110
I feel like I'm back at The Green Dragon...

63
00:09:49,110 --> 00:09:51,620
after a hard day's work.

64
00:09:51,620 --> 00:09:55,600
Only, you've never done a hard day's work.

65
00:10:06,300 --> 00:10:09,510
Welcome, my lords...

66
00:10:09,510 --> 00:10:12,140
...to Isengard!

67
00:10:12,140 --> 00:10:16,060
You young rascals! A merry hunt you've led us on...

68
00:10:16,060 --> 00:10:21,230
and now we find you feasting and...and smoking!

69
00:10:21,230 --> 00:10:24,570
We are sitting on a field of victory...

70
00:10:24,570 --> 00:10:28,590
enjoying a few well-earned comforts.

71
00:10:29,150 --> 00:10:33,510
The salted pork is particularly good.

72
00:10:33,530 --> 00:10:36,430
Salted pork?

73
00:10:36,750 --> 00:10:40,710
-Hobbits.  -We're under orders from Treebeard...

74
00:10:40,710 --> 00:10:44,070
who's taken over management of lsengard.

75
00:10:46,090 --> 00:10:49,260
Young Master Gandalf.

76
00:10:49,260 --> 00:10:54,010
I'm glad you've come.

77
00:10:54,010 --> 00:10:58,600
Wood and water, stock and stone I can master.

78
00:10:58,600 --> 00:11:02,440
But there is a wizard to manage here...

79
00:11:02,440 --> 00:11:04,610
locked in his tower.

80
00:11:04,610 --> 00:11:09,110
And there Saruman must remain under your guard, Treebeard.

81
00:11:09,110 --> 00:11:11,450
Let's just have his head and be done with it.

82
00:11:11,450 --> 00:11:14,010
No.

83
00:11:14,240 --> 00:11:16,790
He has no power anymore.

84
00:11:16,790 --> 00:11:20,880
The filth of Saruman...

85
00:11:20,880 --> 00:11:24,880
is washing away.

86
00:11:24,880 --> 00:11:29,930
Trees will come back to live here.

87
00:11:29,930 --> 00:11:32,260
Young trees.

88
00:11:32,260 --> 00:11:34,990
-Wild trees.  -Pippin!

89
00:11:43,940 --> 00:11:46,280
Bless my bark!

90
00:11:46,280 --> 00:11:48,320
Peregrin Took!

91
00:11:48,320 --> 00:11:51,110
I'll take that, my lad.

92
00:11:51,110 --> 00:11:53,510
Quickly, now.

93
00:12:30,780 --> 00:12:36,850
Tonight we remember those who gave their blood to defend this country.

94
00:12:37,040 --> 00:12:39,210
Hail the victorious dead.

95
00:12:39,210 --> 00:12:42,360
Hail!

96
00:13:28,590 --> 00:13:30,590
I am happy for you.

97
00:13:30,590 --> 00:13:33,430
He is an honorable man.

98
00:13:33,430 --> 00:13:36,410
You are both honorable men.

99
00:13:37,730 --> 00:13:43,590
It was not Theoden of Rohan who led our people to victory.

100
00:13:51,240 --> 00:13:53,600
Don't listen to me.

101
00:13:53,910 --> 00:13:55,620
You are young.

102
00:13:55,620 --> 00:13:57,620
And tonight is for you.

103
00:13:57,620 --> 00:14:02,540
You can search far and wide You can drink the whole town dry

104
00:14:02,540 --> 00:14:06,630
But you'll never find a beer so brown

105
00:14:06,630 --> 00:14:11,220
As the one we drink in our hometown As the one we drink in our hometown

106
00:14:11,220 --> 00:14:15,310
You can drink your fancy ales You can drink 'em by the flagon

107
00:14:15,310 --> 00:14:18,640
But the only brew for the brave and true

108
00:14:18,640 --> 00:14:21,880
Comes from The Green Dragon

109
00:14:24,070 --> 00:14:26,670
Thank you! I win!

110
00:14:28,650 --> 00:14:31,320
No news of Frodo?

111
00:14:31,320 --> 00:14:35,350
No word. Nothing.

112
00:14:35,660 --> 00:14:38,350
We have time.

113
00:14:39,330 --> 00:14:43,150
Every day, Frodo moves closer to Mordor.

114
00:14:43,380 --> 00:14:45,980
Do we know that?

115
00:14:49,300 --> 00:14:52,820
What does your heart tell you?

116
00:14:58,060 --> 00:15:01,920
That Frodo is alive.

117
00:15:03,360 --> 00:15:06,170
Yes.

118
00:15:07,740 --> 00:15:10,640
Yes, he's alive.

119
00:15:12,370 --> 00:15:15,370
Too risky. Too risky.

120
00:15:15,370 --> 00:15:16,790
Thieves.

121
00:15:16,790 --> 00:15:19,000
They stole it from us.

122
00:15:19,000 --> 00:15:22,730
Kill them. Kill them. Kill them both.

123
00:15:24,550 --> 00:15:27,550
Quiet! Mustn't wake them.

124
00:15:27,550 --> 00:15:30,260
Mustn't ruin it now.

125
00:15:30,260 --> 00:15:32,510
But they knows.

126
00:15:32,510 --> 00:15:34,560
They knows.

127
00:15:34,560 --> 00:15:37,710
They suspects us.

128
00:15:38,390 --> 00:15:42,110
What's it saying, my precious, my love?

129
00:15:42,110 --> 00:15:46,210
Is Smeagol losing his nerve?

130
00:15:46,360 --> 00:15:48,900
No. Not.

131
00:15:48,900 --> 00:15:53,330
Never. Smeagol hates nasty Hobbitses.

132
00:15:53,330 --> 00:15:58,330
Smeagol wants to see them dead.

133
00:15:58,330 --> 00:16:01,040
And we will.

134
00:16:01,040 --> 00:16:05,610
Smeagol did it once. He can do it again.

135
00:16:08,420 --> 00:16:11,260
It's ours!

136
00:16:11,260 --> 00:16:14,410
Ours!

137
00:16:15,060 --> 00:16:18,100
We must get the precious. We must get it back.

138
00:16:18,100 --> 00:16:21,690
Patience! Patience, my love.

139
00:16:21,690 --> 00:16:26,590
First we must lead them to her.

140
00:16:26,940 --> 00:16:32,120
We lead them to the Winding Stair.

141
00:16:32,120 --> 00:16:34,950
Yes, the stairs. And then?

142
00:16:34,950 --> 00:16:38,120
Up, up, up, up, up the stairs we go...

143
00:16:38,120 --> 00:16:44,920
until we come to the tunnel.

144
00:16:44,920 --> 00:16:48,220
And when they go in...

145
00:16:48,220 --> 00:16:51,530
...there's no coming out.

146
00:16:51,930 --> 00:16:55,330
She's always hungry.

147
00:16:55,560 --> 00:16:59,940
She always needs to feed.

148
00:16:59,940 --> 00:17:01,520
She must eat.

149
00:17:01,520 --> 00:17:03,820
All she gets is filthy Orcses.

150
00:17:03,820 --> 00:17:06,740
And they doesn't taste very nice, does they, precious?

151
00:17:06,740 --> 00:17:08,990
No.

152
00:17:08,990 --> 00:17:13,870
Not very nice at all, my love.

153
00:17:13,870 --> 00:17:16,830
She hungers for sweeter meats.

154
00:17:16,830 --> 00:17:18,830
Hobbit meat.

155
00:17:18,830 --> 00:17:23,840
And when she throws away the bones and the empty clothes...

156
00:17:23,840 --> 00:17:27,090
then we will find it.

157
00:17:27,090 --> 00:17:31,950
And take it for me!

158
00:17:33,180 --> 00:17:34,760
For us.

159
00:17:34,760 --> 00:17:38,270
Yes. We meant "for us."

160
00:17:38,270 --> 00:17:41,900
Gollum. Gollum.

161
00:17:41,900 --> 00:17:46,570
The precious will be ours...

162
00:17:46,570 --> 00:17:51,590
...once the Hobbitses are dead!

163
00:17:51,620 --> 00:17:53,550
You treacherous little toad!

164
00:17:55,740 --> 00:17:58,210
No! No! Master!

165
00:17:58,210 --> 00:18:00,350
No, Sam! Leave him alone!

166
00:18:00,710 --> 00:18:03,540
I heard it from his own mouth. He means to murder us.

167
00:18:03,540 --> 00:18:08,200
Never! Smeagol wouldn't hurt a fly.

168
00:18:09,220 --> 00:18:11,970
He's a horrid, fat Hobbit...

169
00:18:11,970 --> 00:18:13,720
who hates Smeagol...

170
00:18:13,720 --> 00:18:16,720
and who makes up nasty lies.

171
00:18:16,720 --> 00:18:19,730
You miserable little maggot! I'll stove your head in!

172
00:18:19,730 --> 00:18:21,400
Sam!

173
00:18:21,400 --> 00:18:24,210
Call me a liar? You're a liar!

174
00:18:24,650 --> 00:18:26,500
You scare him off, we're lost!

175
00:18:26,500 --> 00:18:28,740
I don't care! I can't do it, Mr. Frodo.

176
00:18:28,740 --> 00:18:30,610
I won't wait around for him to kill us!

177
00:18:30,610 --> 00:18:32,240
I'm not sending him away.

178
00:18:32,240 --> 00:18:33,990
You don't see it, do you?

179
00:18:33,990 --> 00:18:35,890
He's a villain.

180
00:18:36,410 --> 00:18:40,560
We can't do this by ourselves, Sam. Not without a guide.

181
00:18:40,880 --> 00:18:44,270
I need you on my side.

182
00:18:44,550 --> 00:18:47,400
I'm on your side, Mr. Frodo.

183
00:18:48,380 --> 00:18:51,870
I know, Sam. I know.

184
00:18:51,890 --> 00:18:54,060
Trust me.

185
00:18:54,060 --> 00:18:56,910
Come, Smeagol.

186
00:19:23,540 --> 00:19:26,650
The stars are veiled.

187
00:19:27,130 --> 00:19:31,160
Something stirs in the east.

188
00:19:31,300 --> 00:19:34,950
A sleepless malice.

189
00:19:36,470 --> 00:19:39,750
The Eye of the enemy is moving.

190
00:19:52,490 --> 00:19:55,890
What are you doing?

191
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:02,020
Pippin!

192
00:20:08,470 --> 00:20:10,200
Pippin?

193
00:20:23,650 --> 00:20:25,650
Pippin.

194
00:20:25,650 --> 00:20:28,450
-What, are you mad?  -I just want to look at it.

195
00:20:28,450 --> 00:20:29,860
Just one more time.

196
00:20:29,860 --> 00:20:32,430
Put it back.

197
00:20:42,210 --> 00:20:44,480
Pippin.

198
00:20:50,510 --> 00:20:52,490
No!

199
00:20:57,060 --> 00:20:58,830
Pippin.

200
00:21:01,650 --> 00:21:03,060
He is here.

201
00:21:03,060 --> 00:21:05,880
I see you.

202
00:21:08,110 --> 00:21:10,470
Pippin!

203
00:21:24,590 --> 00:21:27,900
Help! Gandalf, help!

204
00:21:29,090 --> 00:21:31,490
Someone help him!

205
00:21:37,350 --> 00:21:39,080
Pippin!

206
00:21:39,730 --> 00:21:41,460
Fool of a Took!

207
00:22:02,040 --> 00:22:04,770
Look at me.

208
00:22:06,210 --> 00:22:10,510
Gandalf, forgive me.

209
00:22:10,510 --> 00:22:12,600
Look at me.

210
00:22:12,600 --> 00:22:14,950
What did you see?

211
00:22:17,930 --> 00:22:20,500
A tree.

212
00:22:20,980 --> 00:22:22,980
There was a white tree...

213
00:22:22,980 --> 00:22:25,000
...in a courtyard of stone.

214
00:22:27,320 --> 00:22:29,090
It was dead.

215
00:22:32,780 --> 00:22:34,790
The city was burning.

216
00:22:34,790 --> 00:22:38,640
Minas Tirith? Is that what you saw?

217
00:22:38,830 --> 00:22:41,350
I saw....

218
00:22:44,210 --> 00:22:46,150
I saw him.

219
00:22:48,630 --> 00:22:51,010
I could hear his voice in my head.

220
00:22:51,010 --> 00:22:53,640
And what did you tell him?

221
00:22:53,640 --> 00:22:56,620
Speak!

222
00:22:59,600 --> 00:23:02,940
He asked me my name. I didn't answer.

223
00:23:02,940 --> 00:23:04,570
He hurt me.

224
00:23:04,570 --> 00:23:07,550
What did you tell him about Frodo and the Ring?

225
00:23:10,530 --> 00:23:13,550
There was no lie in Pippin's eyes.

226
00:23:13,870 --> 00:23:16,250
A fool...

227
00:23:16,250 --> 00:23:18,710
but an honest fool he remains.

228
00:23:18,710 --> 00:23:23,060
He told Sauron nothing of Frodo and the Ring.

229
00:23:23,590 --> 00:23:26,170
We've been strangely fortunate.

230
00:23:26,170 --> 00:23:30,530
Pippin saw in the palantir a glimpse of the enemy's plan.

231
00:23:30,930 --> 00:23:35,410
Sauron moves to strike the city of Minas Tirith.

232
00:23:35,520 --> 00:23:39,390
His defeat at Helm's Deep showed our enemy one thing.

233
00:23:39,390 --> 00:23:41,900
He knows the heir of Elendil has come forth.

234
00:23:41,900 --> 00:23:44,230
Men are not as weak as he supposed.

235
00:23:44,230 --> 00:23:48,240
There is courage still, strength enough perhaps to challenge him.

236
00:23:48,240 --> 00:23:50,240
Sauron fears this.

237
00:23:50,240 --> 00:23:55,100
He will not risk the peoples of Middle-earth uniting under one banner.

238
00:23:55,740 --> 00:23:58,330
He will raze Minas Tirith to the ground...

239
00:23:58,330 --> 00:24:02,000
before he sees a king return to the throne of Men.

240
00:24:02,000 --> 00:24:06,440
If the beacons of Gondor are lit, Rohan must be ready for war.

241
00:24:06,880 --> 00:24:09,260
Tell me...

242
00:24:09,260 --> 00:24:13,580
why should we ride to the aid of those who did not come to ours?

243
00:24:16,930 --> 00:24:19,250
What do we owe Gondor?

244
00:24:19,890 --> 00:24:22,110
-I will go.  -No!

245
00:24:22,110 --> 00:24:25,760
-They must be warned.  -They will be.

246
00:24:28,650 --> 00:24:31,720
You must come to Minas Tirith by another road.

247
00:24:31,780 --> 00:24:36,720
Follow the river and look to the black ships.

248
00:24:37,160 --> 00:24:39,290
Understand this:

249
00:24:39,290 --> 00:24:43,480
Things are now in motion that cannot be undone.

250
00:24:44,460 --> 00:24:47,110
I ride for Minas Tirith...

251
00:24:48,800 --> 00:24:51,990
...and I won't be going alone.

252
00:24:53,220 --> 00:24:57,450
Of all the inquisitive Hobbits, Peregrin Took, you are the worst.

253
00:24:57,930 --> 00:25:00,120
Hurry! Hurry!

254
00:25:01,060 --> 00:25:02,650
Where are we going?

255
00:25:02,650 --> 00:25:04,070
Why did you look?

256
00:25:04,070 --> 00:25:06,990
Why do you always have to look?

257
00:25:06,990 --> 00:25:10,530
-I don't know. I can't help it.  -You never can.

258
00:25:10,530 --> 00:25:12,510
I'm sorry, all right?

259
00:25:14,030 --> 00:25:17,520
-I won't do it again.  -Don't you understand?

260
00:25:17,710 --> 00:25:19,830
The enemy thinks you have the Ring.

261
00:25:19,830 --> 00:25:24,150
He's going to be looking for you, Pip. They have to get you out of here.

262
00:25:25,000 --> 00:25:28,200
And you...? You're coming with me?

263
00:25:29,880 --> 00:25:31,510
Merry?

264
00:25:31,510 --> 00:25:33,330
Come on.

265
00:25:38,310 --> 00:25:39,850
How far is Minas Tirith?

266
00:25:39,850 --> 00:25:42,650
Three days' ride, as the Nazgul flies.

267
00:25:42,650 --> 00:25:46,630
And you better hope we don't have one of those on our tail.

268
00:25:46,860 --> 00:25:48,530
Here.

269
00:25:48,530 --> 00:25:50,800
Something for the road.

270
00:25:51,200 --> 00:25:53,330
The last of the Longbottom Leaf.

271
00:25:53,330 --> 00:25:57,500
I know you've run out. You smoke too much, Pippin.

272
00:25:57,500 --> 00:26:00,480
But...But we'll see each other soon.

273
00:26:03,340 --> 00:26:06,320
-Won't we?  -I don't know.

274
00:26:07,800 --> 00:26:10,050
I don't know what's going to happen.

275
00:26:10,050 --> 00:26:11,890
-Merry.  -Run, Shadowfax.

276
00:26:11,890 --> 00:26:13,550
Show us the meaning of haste.

277
00:26:13,550 --> 00:26:15,950
Merry!

278
00:26:25,730 --> 00:26:27,550
Merry!

279
00:26:53,050 --> 00:26:55,520
Take her by the safest road.

280
00:26:55,520 --> 00:26:58,180
A ship lies anchored in the Grey Havens.

281
00:26:58,180 --> 00:27:02,230
It waits to carry her across the sea.

282
00:27:02,230 --> 00:27:06,380
The last journey of Arwen Undomiel.

283
00:28:11,220 --> 00:28:14,830
There is nothing for you here...

284
00:28:14,850 --> 00:28:17,540
only death.

285
00:28:24,320 --> 00:28:26,130
Lady Arwen...

286
00:28:26,530 --> 00:28:28,970
we cannot delay.

287
00:28:30,910 --> 00:28:32,680
My lady!

288
00:28:51,550 --> 00:28:54,350
-Tell me what you have seen.  -Arwen.

289
00:28:54,350 --> 00:28:56,470
You have the gift of foresight.

290
00:28:56,470 --> 00:28:58,790
What did you see?

291
00:28:58,890 --> 00:29:02,750
I looked into your future, and I saw death.

292
00:29:02,770 --> 00:29:05,420
But there is also life.

293
00:29:06,820 --> 00:29:11,340
You saw there was a child. You saw my son.

294
00:29:11,490 --> 00:29:14,240
That future is almost gone.

295
00:29:14,240 --> 00:29:16,720
But it is not lost.

296
00:29:18,790 --> 00:29:21,520
Nothing is certain.

297
00:29:22,750 --> 00:29:25,940
Some things are certain.

298
00:29:29,220 --> 00:29:32,260
If I leave him now...

299
00:29:32,260 --> 00:29:35,370
...I will regret it forever.

300
00:29:35,930 --> 00:29:38,790
It is time.

301
00:29:43,520 --> 00:29:47,490
From the ashes a fire shall be woken

302
00:29:47,490 --> 00:29:51,070
A light from the shadow shall spring

303
00:29:51,070 --> 00:29:54,890
Renewed shall be blade that was broken

304
00:30:01,460 --> 00:30:05,480
The crownless again shall be king

305
00:30:08,470 --> 00:30:11,280
Re-forge the sword.

306
00:30:45,460 --> 00:30:48,860
Your hands are cold.

307
00:30:51,510 --> 00:30:55,370
The life of the Eldar is leaving you.

308
00:30:58,270 --> 00:31:00,710
This was my choice.

309
00:31:02,020 --> 00:31:04,840
Whether by your will or not...

310
00:31:05,650 --> 00:31:10,470
...there is no ship now that can bear me hence.

311
00:31:57,160 --> 00:32:00,520
We've just passed into the realm of Gondor.

312
00:32:11,390 --> 00:32:14,100
Minas Tirith.

313
00:32:14,100 --> 00:32:17,330
City of kings.

314
00:32:48,220 --> 00:32:50,530
Make way!

315
00:33:19,210 --> 00:33:21,210
It's the tree.

316
00:33:21,210 --> 00:33:23,040
Gandalf. Gandalf.

317
00:33:23,040 --> 00:33:25,500
Yes, the White Tree of Gondor.

318
00:33:25,500 --> 00:33:27,470
The tree of the king.

319
00:33:27,470 --> 00:33:30,300
Lord Denethor, however, is not king.

320
00:33:30,300 --> 00:33:33,490
He is a steward only, a caretaker of the throne.

321
00:33:33,720 --> 00:33:37,790
Now listen carefully. Lord Denethor is Boromir's father.

322
00:33:37,810 --> 00:33:42,060
To give him news of his beloved son's death would be most unwise.

323
00:33:42,060 --> 00:33:46,050
And do not mention Frodo or the Ring.

324
00:33:46,400 --> 00:33:49,680
And say nothing of Aragorn either.

325
00:33:50,990 --> 00:33:55,390
In fact, it's better if you don't speak at all, Peregrin Took.

326
00:34:25,030 --> 00:34:32,010
Hail Denethor, son of Ecthelion, lord and steward of Gondor.

327
00:34:37,040 --> 00:34:42,270
I come with tidings in this dark hour, and with counsel.

328
00:34:42,750 --> 00:34:46,610
Perhaps you come to explain this.

329
00:34:51,720 --> 00:34:56,790
Perhaps you come to tell me why my son is dead.

330
00:35:10,740 --> 00:35:13,950
Boromir died to save us...

331
00:35:13,950 --> 00:35:15,740
my kinsman and me.

332
00:35:15,740 --> 00:35:19,730
-He fell defending us from many foes.  -Pippin.

333
00:35:24,750 --> 00:35:28,740
I offer you my service, such as it is...

334
00:35:28,800 --> 00:35:32,120
in payment of this debt.

335
00:35:33,140 --> 00:35:35,060
Get up.

336
00:35:35,060 --> 00:35:40,150
My lord, there will be a time to grieve for Boromir...

337
00:35:40,150 --> 00:35:42,420
...but it is not now.

338
00:35:42,610 --> 00:35:45,150
War is coming.

339
00:35:45,150 --> 00:35:49,740
The enemy is on your doorstep. As steward, you are charged

340
00:35:49,740 --> 00:35:54,030
with the defense of this city. Where are Gondor's armies?

341
00:35:54,030 --> 00:35:59,120
You still have friends. You are not alone in this fight.

342
00:35:59,120 --> 00:36:04,110
Send word to Theoden of Rohan. Light the beacons.

343
00:36:05,170 --> 00:36:08,880
You think you are wise, Mithrandir.

344
00:36:08,880 --> 00:36:12,450
Yet for all your subtleties, you have not wisdom.

345
00:36:14,100 --> 00:36:18,430
Do you think the eyes of the White Tower are blind?

346
00:36:18,430 --> 00:36:21,690
I have seen more than you know.

347
00:36:21,690 --> 00:36:25,030
With your left hand you would use me as a shield against Mordor.

348
00:36:25,030 --> 00:36:28,110
And with your right you'd seek to supplant me.

349
00:36:28,110 --> 00:36:31,990
I know who rides with Theoden of Rohan.

350
00:36:31,990 --> 00:36:38,080
yes. Word has reached my ears of this Aragorn, son of Arathorn.

351
00:36:38,080 --> 00:36:43,130
And I tell you now, I will not bow to this Ranger from the North...

352
00:36:43,130 --> 00:36:47,800
last of a ragged house long bereft of lordship.

353
00:36:47,800 --> 00:36:53,760
Authority is not given to you to deny the return of the king, steward.

354
00:36:53,760 --> 00:36:58,750
The rule of Gondor is mine and no other's.

355
00:37:03,400 --> 00:37:05,710
Come.

356
00:37:17,450 --> 00:37:22,000
So I imagine this is just a ceremonial position.

357
00:37:22,000 --> 00:37:26,420
I mean, they don't actually expect me to do any fighting.

358
00:37:26,420 --> 00:37:31,260
-Do they?  -You're in the service of the steward now.

359
00:37:31,260 --> 00:37:38,210
You're going to have to do as you're told, Peregrin Took, guard of the Citadel.

360
00:37:40,480 --> 00:37:43,150
It's so quiet.

361
00:37:43,150 --> 00:37:47,920
It's the deep breath before the plunge.

362
00:37:48,610 --> 00:37:51,970
I don't want to be in a battle...

363
00:37:52,280 --> 00:37:57,770
but waiting on the edge of one I can't escape is even worse.

364
00:38:00,790 --> 00:38:04,940
Is there any hope, Gandalf, for Frodo and Sam?

365
00:38:05,760 --> 00:38:09,400
There never was much hope.

366
00:38:10,590 --> 00:38:13,990
Just a fool's hope.

367
00:38:18,480 --> 00:38:21,480
Our enemy is ready.

368
00:38:21,480 --> 00:38:24,270
His full strength's gathered.

369
00:38:24,270 --> 00:38:27,940
Not only Orcs, but Men as well.

370
00:38:27,940 --> 00:38:31,160
Legions of Haradrim from the south...

371
00:38:31,160 --> 00:38:34,030
...mercenaries from the coast.

372
00:38:34,030 --> 00:38:36,790
All will answer Mordor's call.

373
00:38:36,790 --> 00:38:38,850
Come on.

374
00:38:39,500 --> 00:38:42,960
This will be the end of Gondor as we know it.

375
00:38:42,960 --> 00:38:46,860
Here the hammer stroke will fall hardest.

376
00:38:47,300 --> 00:38:51,800
If the river is taken, if the garrison at Osgiliath falls...

377
00:38:51,800 --> 00:38:55,640
the last defense of this city will be gone.

378
00:38:55,640 --> 00:39:00,210
But we have the White Wizard. That's got to count for something.

379
00:39:05,570 --> 00:39:07,670
Gandalf?

380
00:39:10,860 --> 00:39:15,040
Sauron has yet to reveal his deadliest servant...

381
00:39:15,040 --> 00:39:19,000
the one who will lead Mordor's armies in war.

382
00:39:19,000 --> 00:39:24,690
The one they say no living man can kill.

383
00:39:25,210 --> 00:39:27,860
The Witch-king of Angmar.

384
00:39:28,420 --> 00:39:31,320
You've met him before.

385
00:39:31,470 --> 00:39:34,580
He stabbed Frodo on Weathertop.

386
00:39:40,600 --> 00:39:43,770
He is the lord of the Nazgul...

387
00:39:43,770 --> 00:39:46,400
...the greatest of the Nine.

388
00:39:46,400 --> 00:39:51,340
Minas Morgul is his lair.

389
00:39:53,490 --> 00:39:57,200
The Dead City.

390
00:39:57,200 --> 00:40:02,940
Very nasty place. Full of enemies.

391
00:40:09,630 --> 00:40:11,970
Quick. Quick.

392
00:40:11,970 --> 00:40:16,500
They will see. They will see.

393
00:40:25,230 --> 00:40:30,700
Come away. Come away. Look, we have found it.

394
00:40:30,700 --> 00:40:34,740
The way into Mordor.

395
00:40:34,740 --> 00:40:39,500
The secret stair.

396
00:40:39,500 --> 00:40:42,400
Climb.

397
00:41:02,150 --> 00:41:05,420
-No, Mr. Frodo!  -Not that way!

398
00:41:09,740 --> 00:41:12,490
-What's it doing?  -No.

399
00:41:12,490 --> 00:41:16,390
-They're calling me.  -No.

400
00:41:45,530 --> 00:41:49,010
Hide! Hide!

401
00:42:31,910 --> 00:42:35,390
I can feel his blade.

402
00:42:46,590 --> 00:42:50,240
We come to it at last.

403
00:42:50,510 --> 00:42:53,910
The great battle of our time.

404
00:43:32,550 --> 00:43:36,330
Come away, Hobbits. We climb. We must climb.

405
00:43:45,650 --> 00:43:48,860
The board is set.

406
00:43:48,860 --> 00:43:51,930
The pieces are moving.

407
00:43:52,320 --> 00:43:55,330
Peregrin Took, my lad, there is a task now to be done.

408
00:43:55,330 --> 00:44:00,480
Another opportunity for one of the Shire-folk to prove their great worth.

409
00:44:04,800 --> 00:44:06,860
You must not fail me.

410
00:44:48,840 --> 00:44:50,550
Quiet.

411
00:44:50,550 --> 00:44:53,890
-To the river. Quick. Quick.  -Go. Go.

412
00:44:53,890 --> 00:44:55,700
Come on.

413
00:44:58,180 --> 00:45:00,420
Faster.

414
00:45:13,080 --> 00:45:15,930
Draw swords.

415
00:46:09,970 --> 00:46:13,080
Hold! Hold!

416
00:47:32,890 --> 00:47:35,240
What?

417
00:47:47,280 --> 00:47:50,720
Amon Din.

418
00:47:54,540 --> 00:47:58,060
The beacon. The beacon of Amon Din is lit.

419
00:48:00,790 --> 00:48:05,570
Hope is kindled.

420
00:49:37,390 --> 00:49:42,330
The beacons of Minas Tirith! The beacons are lit!

421
00:49:43,020 --> 00:49:46,170
Gondor calls for aid.

422
00:49:55,160 --> 00:49:58,500
And Rohan will answer.

423
00:49:58,500 --> 00:50:01,770
Muster the Rohirrim.

424
00:50:16,390 --> 00:50:18,480
Assemble the army at Dunharrow.

425
00:50:18,480 --> 00:50:23,060
As many men as can be found. You have two days.

426
00:50:23,060 --> 00:50:28,840
On the third, we ride for Gondor and war.

427
00:50:29,280 --> 00:50:30,780
-Forward.  -Very good, sir.

428
00:50:30,780 --> 00:50:32,280
-Gamling.  -My lord.

429
00:50:32,280 --> 00:50:34,080
Make haste across the Riddermark.

430
00:50:34,080 --> 00:50:36,330
Summon every able-bodied man to Dunharrow.

431
00:50:36,330 --> 00:50:38,980
I will.

432
00:50:42,040 --> 00:50:45,380
-Will you ride with us?  -Just to the encampment.

433
00:50:45,380 --> 00:50:49,780
It's tradition for the women of the court to farewell the men.

434
00:50:55,810 --> 00:50:57,930
The men have found their captain.

435
00:50:57,930 --> 00:51:01,440
They will follow you into battle, even to death.

436
00:51:01,440 --> 00:51:04,550
You have given us hope.

437
00:51:18,410 --> 00:51:22,040
So it is before the walls of Minas Tirith...

438
00:51:22,040 --> 00:51:26,440
...the doom of our time will be decided.

439
00:51:28,510 --> 00:51:34,220
Now is the hour. Riders of Rohan, oaths you have taken.

440
00:51:34,220 --> 00:51:38,290
Now, fulfill them all. to lord and land!

441
00:52:20,850 --> 00:52:23,380
Faramir!

442
00:52:29,110 --> 00:52:33,350
We can't hold them. The city is lost.

443
00:52:33,410 --> 00:52:36,980
Tell the men to break cover. We ride for Minas Tirith.

444
00:52:45,250 --> 00:52:48,030
Nazgul.

445
00:52:49,880 --> 00:52:52,550
Take cover!

446
00:52:52,550 --> 00:52:55,220
Nazgul!

447
00:52:55,220 --> 00:52:59,420
Fall back. Fall back to Minas Tirith!

448
00:53:05,480 --> 00:53:07,880
Fall back!

449
00:53:14,410 --> 00:53:19,520
-Retreat! Retreat!  -Come on!

450
00:53:43,270 --> 00:53:47,780
The age of Men is over.

451
00:53:47,780 --> 00:53:53,890
The time of the Orc has come.

452
00:53:55,740 --> 00:53:58,600
Take cover!

453
00:53:59,710 --> 00:54:02,380
Take cover, my lord!

454
00:54:02,380 --> 00:54:04,230
It's coming!

455
00:54:09,300 --> 00:54:13,160
-It's Mithrandir.  -The White Rider!

456
00:54:52,600 --> 00:54:54,490
Pull!

457
00:55:11,700 --> 00:55:14,280
Mithrandir.

458
00:55:14,280 --> 00:55:16,200
They broke through our defenses.

459
00:55:16,200 --> 00:55:18,940
They've taken the bridge and the west bank.

460
00:55:19,540 --> 00:55:21,630
Battalions of Orcs are crossing the river.

461
00:55:21,630 --> 00:55:23,840
It is as the Lord Denethor predicted.

462
00:55:23,840 --> 00:55:28,900
-Long has he foreseen this doom.  -Foreseen and done nothing.

463
00:55:31,760 --> 00:55:34,700
Faramir?

464
00:55:36,100 --> 00:55:40,100
This is not the first Halfling to have crossed your path.

465
00:55:40,100 --> 00:55:42,840
No.

466
00:55:43,650 --> 00:55:45,670
You've seen Frodo and Sam?

467
00:55:46,070 --> 00:55:49,650
-Where? When?  -In Ithilien.

468
00:55:49,650 --> 00:55:52,200
Not two days ago.

469
00:55:52,200 --> 00:55:57,180
Gandalf, they're taking the road to the Morgul Vale.

470
00:55:57,410 --> 00:56:00,520
And then the pass of Cirith Ungol.

471
00:56:02,000 --> 00:56:04,750
What does that mean?

472
00:56:04,750 --> 00:56:10,200
-What's wrong?  -Faramir, tell me everything.

473
00:56:37,160 --> 00:56:40,080
Careful, master. Careful.

474
00:56:40,080 --> 00:56:43,940
Very far to fall.

475
00:56:45,670 --> 00:56:50,110
Very dangerous are the stairs.

476
00:56:52,300 --> 00:56:55,330
Come, master.

477
00:57:00,650 --> 00:57:04,300
Come to Smeagol.

478
00:57:10,110 --> 00:57:12,140
Mr. Frodo.

479
00:57:12,620 --> 00:57:14,330
Get back, you!

480
00:57:14,330 --> 00:57:17,060
Don't touch him!

481
00:57:20,670 --> 00:57:23,670
Why does he hates poor Smeagol?

482
00:57:23,670 --> 00:57:27,550
What has Smeagol ever done to him?

483
00:57:27,550 --> 00:57:30,450
Master?

484
00:57:30,720 --> 00:57:34,350
Master carries heavy burden.

485
00:57:34,350 --> 00:57:39,940
Smeagol knows. Heavy, heavy burden.

486
00:57:39,940 --> 00:57:43,710
Fat one cannot know.

487
00:57:45,230 --> 00:57:48,510
Smeagol look after master.

488
00:57:49,200 --> 00:57:51,570
He wants it.

489
00:57:51,570 --> 00:57:56,290
He needs it. Smeagol sees it in his eye.

490
00:57:56,290 --> 00:58:01,920
Very soon he will ask you for it. You will see.

491
00:58:01,920 --> 00:58:06,320
The fat one will take it from you.

492
00:58:13,010 --> 00:58:17,560
Send forth all legions.

493
00:58:17,560 --> 00:58:22,080
Do not stop the attack until the city is taken.

494
00:58:22,270 --> 00:58:25,920
Slay them all.

495
00:58:27,070 --> 00:58:33,390
-What of the wizard?  -I will break him.

496
00:58:36,200 --> 00:58:38,790
What of Theoden's riders?

497
00:58:38,790 --> 00:58:41,580
Will Rohan's army come?

498
00:58:41,580 --> 00:58:44,320
Mithrandir.

499
00:58:44,840 --> 00:58:49,240
Courage is the best defense that you have now.

500
00:58:49,430 --> 00:58:53,390
Here do I swear feaIty and service to Gondor...

501
00:58:53,390 --> 00:58:55,410
...in peace or war...

502
00:58:55,560 --> 00:58:58,540
...in living or dying...

503
00:58:59,390 --> 00:59:01,130
from...

504
00:59:03,270 --> 00:59:06,230
From this hour henceforth...

505
00:59:06,230 --> 00:59:08,720
until my lord release me...

506
00:59:09,700 --> 00:59:12,430
or death take me.

507
00:59:12,450 --> 00:59:15,120
And I shall not forget it...

508
00:59:15,120 --> 00:59:19,060
nor fail to reward that which is given.

509
00:59:26,130 --> 00:59:28,950
Fealty with love.

510
00:59:29,470 --> 00:59:31,660
Valor with honor.

511
00:59:32,760 --> 00:59:36,620
DisloyaIty with vengeance.

512
00:59:44,730 --> 00:59:48,990
I do not think we should so lightly abandon the outer defenses

513
00:59:48,990 --> 00:59:51,910
defenses that your brother long held intact.

514
00:59:51,910 --> 00:59:54,580
-What would you have me do?  -I will not yield...

515
00:59:54,580 --> 00:59:57,500
the river in Pelennor unfought.

516
00:59:57,500 --> 00:59:59,330
Osgiliath must be retaken.

517
00:59:59,330 --> 01:00:01,940
My lord, Osgiliath is overrun.

518
01:00:02,080 --> 01:00:05,360
Much must be risked in war.

519
01:00:07,470 --> 01:00:11,950
Is there a captain here who still has the courage to do his lord's will?

520
01:00:17,640 --> 01:00:21,460
You wish now that our places had been exchanged...

521
01:00:21,860 --> 01:00:25,210
that I had died and Boromir had lived.

522
01:00:28,150 --> 01:00:30,380
Yes.

523
01:00:30,570 --> 01:00:33,300
I wish that.

524
01:00:41,170 --> 01:00:44,150
Since you were robbed of Boromir...

525
01:00:45,500 --> 01:00:48,900
...I will do what I can in his stead.

526
01:00:56,560 --> 01:01:01,540
If I should return, think better of me, Father.

527
01:01:03,150 --> 01:01:07,260
That will depend on the manner of your return.

528
01:02:30,070 --> 01:02:32,570
What are you up to?

529
01:02:32,570 --> 01:02:34,310
Sneaking off, are we?

530
01:02:34,540 --> 01:02:36,850
Sneaking?

531
01:02:37,370 --> 01:02:40,060
Sneaking?

532
01:02:40,960 --> 01:02:44,300
Fat Hobbit is always so polite.

533
01:02:44,300 --> 01:02:49,550
Smeagol shows them secret ways that nobody else could find...

534
01:02:49,550 --> 01:02:52,200
and they say "sneak. "

535
01:02:52,350 --> 01:02:55,450
Sneak?

536
01:02:55,520 --> 01:02:58,430
Very nice friend. Oh, yes, my precious.

537
01:02:58,430 --> 01:03:01,540
-Very nice, very nice.  -All right. All right!

538
01:03:02,310 --> 01:03:04,980
You just startled me is all.

539
01:03:04,980 --> 01:03:07,340
What were you doing?

540
01:03:08,490 --> 01:03:10,990
Sneaking.

541
01:03:10,990 --> 01:03:14,560
Fine. Have it your own way.

542
01:03:16,330 --> 01:03:19,210
I'm sorry to wake you, Mr. Frodo.

543
01:03:19,210 --> 01:03:21,690
We have to be moving on.

544
01:03:26,340 --> 01:03:28,050
It's dark still.

545
01:03:28,050 --> 01:03:30,820
It's always dark here.

546
01:03:34,510 --> 01:03:37,000
It's gone!

547
01:03:37,680 --> 01:03:40,690
-The Elven bread.  -What?

548
01:03:40,690 --> 01:03:42,710
That's all we have left.

549
01:03:46,230 --> 01:03:49,240
He took it. He must have!

550
01:03:49,240 --> 01:03:52,700
Smeagol? No, no, not poor Smeagol.

551
01:03:52,700 --> 01:03:55,740
Smeagol hates nasty Elf bread.

552
01:03:55,740 --> 01:03:59,120
You're a lying wretch! What did you do with it?!

553
01:03:59,120 --> 01:04:01,190
He doesn't eat it.

554
01:04:01,670 --> 01:04:04,520
-He can't have taken it.  -Look.

555
01:04:05,050 --> 01:04:07,400
What's this?

556
01:04:09,550 --> 01:04:13,410
Crumbs on his jacketses. He took it!

557
01:04:13,550 --> 01:04:15,740
He took it.

558
01:04:16,060 --> 01:04:20,440
I seen him. He's always stuffing his face when master's not looking.

559
01:04:20,440 --> 01:04:22,440
That's a filthy lie!

560
01:04:22,440 --> 01:04:24,820
You stinking, two-faced sneak!

561
01:04:24,820 --> 01:04:26,230
-Sam!  -Call me...

562
01:04:26,230 --> 01:04:27,970
Stop it!

563
01:04:28,450 --> 01:04:30,220
Sam!

564
01:04:30,950 --> 01:04:35,100
-I'll kill him!  -Sam! No!

565
01:04:35,620 --> 01:04:41,380
I'm sorry. I didn't mean it to go so far. I was just so...So angry.

566
01:04:41,380 --> 01:04:43,670
Here, just...Let's just rest a bit.

567
01:04:43,670 --> 01:04:45,920
-I'm all right.  -No.

568
01:04:45,920 --> 01:04:49,180
No, you're not all right. You're exhausted.

569
01:04:49,180 --> 01:04:51,470
It's that Gollum.

570
01:04:51,470 --> 01:04:53,350
It's this place.

571
01:04:53,350 --> 01:04:56,410
It's that thing around your neck.

572
01:04:59,440 --> 01:05:00,900
I could help a bit.

573
01:05:00,900 --> 01:05:03,730
I could carry it for a while.

574
01:05:03,730 --> 01:05:05,610
Carry it for a while.

575
01:05:05,610 --> 01:05:07,420
I could carry it...I could carry it.

576
01:05:07,530 --> 01:05:13,120
Share the load...Share the load...the load...the load.

577
01:05:13,120 --> 01:05:14,540
Get away!

578
01:05:14,540 --> 01:05:16,600
I don't want to keep it.

579
01:05:19,670 --> 01:05:22,190
I just want to help.

580
01:05:23,750 --> 01:05:26,510
See? See?

581
01:05:26,510 --> 01:05:30,130
He wants it for himseIf.

582
01:05:30,130 --> 01:05:32,320
Shut up, you!

583
01:05:32,350 --> 01:05:34,390
Go away! Get out of here!

584
01:05:34,390 --> 01:05:36,390
No, Sam.

585
01:05:36,390 --> 01:05:38,160
It's you.

586
01:05:41,810 --> 01:05:44,040
I'm sorry, Sam.

587
01:05:45,280 --> 01:05:46,780
But he's a liar.

588
01:05:46,780 --> 01:05:49,970
He's poisoned you against me.

589
01:05:50,820 --> 01:05:53,300
You can't help me anymore.

590
01:05:54,740 --> 01:05:57,140
You don't mean that.

591
01:05:59,120 --> 01:06:01,440
Go home.

592
01:07:20,920 --> 01:07:22,920
Faramir!

593
01:07:22,920 --> 01:07:25,320
Faramir!

594
01:07:26,340 --> 01:07:28,900
Your father's will has turned to madness.

595
01:07:29,550 --> 01:07:32,070
Do not throw away your life so rashly.

596
01:07:32,350 --> 01:07:35,160
Where does my allegiance lie if not here?

597
01:07:39,390 --> 01:07:43,290
Your father loves you, Faramir.

598
01:07:43,480 --> 01:07:47,050
He will remember it before the end.

599
01:08:56,140 --> 01:08:58,160
Can you sing, Master Hobbit?

600
01:09:00,520 --> 01:09:02,540
Well...

601
01:09:02,610 --> 01:09:04,710
...yes.

602
01:09:04,900 --> 01:09:09,220
At least, well enough for my own people.

603
01:09:10,320 --> 01:09:13,220
But we have no songs for great halls...

604
01:09:13,740 --> 01:09:15,560
...and evil times.

605
01:09:15,870 --> 01:09:19,560
And why should your songs be unfit for my halls?

606
01:09:21,830 --> 01:09:23,730
Come, sing me a song.

607
01:09:34,260 --> 01:09:37,810
Home is behind

608
01:09:37,810 --> 01:09:42,080
The world ahead

609
01:09:43,940 --> 01:09:50,300
And there are many paths to tread

610
01:09:51,570 --> 01:09:55,330
Through shadow

611
01:09:55,330 --> 01:09:59,980
To the edge of night

612
01:10:01,170 --> 01:10:06,740
Until the stars are all alight

613
01:10:09,260 --> 01:10:13,760
Mist and shadow

614
01:10:13,760 --> 01:10:18,580
Cloud and shade

615
01:10:20,440 --> 01:10:24,300
All shall fade

616
01:10:26,110 --> 01:10:30,640
All shall

617
01:10:35,910 --> 01:10:38,810
Fade

618
01:11:02,650 --> 01:11:06,320
March! March!

619
01:11:06,320 --> 01:11:12,010
March! March! March!

620
01:11:14,990 --> 01:11:17,850
Make way for the king.

621
01:11:18,830 --> 01:11:21,310
Make way.

622
01:11:23,290 --> 01:11:25,820
The king is here.

623
01:11:27,300 --> 01:11:29,450
My lord.

624
01:11:30,180 --> 01:11:32,550
Hail to you, sire.

625
01:11:32,550 --> 01:11:33,970
Grimbold, how many?

626
01:11:33,970 --> 01:11:36,910
I bring 500 men from the Westfold, my lord.

627
01:11:37,350 --> 01:11:40,540
We have 300 more from Fenmarch, Theoden King.

628
01:11:41,190 --> 01:11:45,670
-Where are the riders from Snowbourn?  -None have come, my lord.

629
01:12:02,210 --> 01:12:04,860
Six thousand spears.

630
01:12:05,380 --> 01:12:07,670
Less than half of what I'd hoped for.

631
01:12:07,670 --> 01:12:11,570
Six thousand will not be enough to break the lines of Mordor.

632
01:12:13,760 --> 01:12:15,890
More will come.

633
01:12:15,890 --> 01:12:19,060
Every hour lost hastens Gondor's defeat.

634
01:12:19,060 --> 01:12:22,130
We have till dawn, then we must ride.

635
01:12:41,080 --> 01:12:43,590
The horses are restless...

636
01:12:43,590 --> 01:12:45,590
...and the men are quiet.

637
01:12:45,590 --> 01:12:49,240
They grow nervous in the shadow of the mountain.

638
01:12:51,180 --> 01:12:53,580
That road there...

639
01:12:53,930 --> 01:12:56,580
...where does that lead?

640
01:12:56,770 --> 01:13:01,130
It is the road to the Dimholt, the door under the mountain.

641
01:13:01,350 --> 01:13:04,880
None who venture there ever return.

642
01:13:05,570 --> 01:13:07,970
That mountain is evil.

643
01:13:30,340 --> 01:13:32,700
Aragorn.

644
01:13:32,930 --> 01:13:35,370
Let's find some food.

645
01:13:51,320 --> 01:13:53,260
There.

646
01:13:53,700 --> 01:13:57,230
A true esquire of Rohan.

647
01:14:00,330 --> 01:14:02,810
I'm ready.

648
01:14:03,920 --> 01:14:05,380
Sorry.

649
01:14:05,380 --> 01:14:08,130
It isn't all that dangerous.

650
01:14:08,130 --> 01:14:10,990
It's not even sharp.

651
01:14:11,140 --> 01:14:14,720
that's no good. You won't kill many Orcs with a blunt blade.

652
01:14:14,720 --> 01:14:16,700
Come on.

653
01:14:20,400 --> 01:14:23,420
To the smithy. Go!

654
01:14:24,360 --> 01:14:27,070
You should not encourage him.

655
01:14:27,070 --> 01:14:29,700
You should not doubt him.

656
01:14:29,700 --> 01:14:33,510
I do not doubt his heart, only the reach of his arm.

657
01:14:35,700 --> 01:14:37,450
Why should Merry be left behind?

658
01:14:37,450 --> 01:14:40,600
He has as much cause to go to war as you.

659
01:14:42,250 --> 01:14:45,900
Why can he not fight for those he loves?

660
01:15:14,620 --> 01:15:18,810
I choose a mortal life.

661
01:15:21,210 --> 01:15:24,650
I wish I could've seen him...

662
01:15:25,210 --> 01:15:28,450
...one last time.

663
01:15:39,100 --> 01:15:41,040
Sir?

664
01:15:42,360 --> 01:15:45,460
King Theoden awaits you, my lord.

665
01:16:05,710 --> 01:16:08,200
I take my leave.

666
01:16:22,360 --> 01:16:24,090
My lord Elrond.

667
01:16:24,190 --> 01:16:28,130
I come on behalf of one whom I love.

668
01:16:30,740 --> 01:16:33,260
Arwen is dying.

669
01:16:37,540 --> 01:16:42,110
She will not long survive the evil that now spreads from Mordor.

670
01:16:42,330 --> 01:16:45,880
The light of the Evenstar is failing.

671
01:16:45,880 --> 01:16:50,050
As Sauron's power grows, her strength wanes.

672
01:16:50,050 --> 01:16:54,330
Arwen's life is now tied to the fate of the Ring.

673
01:16:54,560 --> 01:16:57,520
The Shadow is upon us, Aragorn.

674
01:16:57,520 --> 01:16:59,560
The end has come.

675
01:16:59,560 --> 01:17:02,710
It will not be our end, but his.

676
01:17:02,940 --> 01:17:07,050
You ride to war, but not to victory.

677
01:17:07,570 --> 01:17:11,410
Sauron's armies march on Minas Tirith, this you know.

678
01:17:11,410 --> 01:17:16,250
But in secret he sends another force which will attack from the river.

679
01:17:16,250 --> 01:17:20,190
A fleet of Corsairs ships sails from the south.

680
01:17:20,290 --> 01:17:22,880
They'll be in the city in two days.

681
01:17:22,880 --> 01:17:26,230
You're outnumbered, Aragorn.

682
01:17:26,420 --> 01:17:28,930
You need more men.

683
01:17:28,930 --> 01:17:31,200
There are none.

684
01:17:32,430 --> 01:17:36,870
There are those who dwell in the mountain.

685
01:17:45,360 --> 01:17:47,690
Murderers...

686
01:17:47,690 --> 01:17:49,630
traitors.

687
01:17:51,570 --> 01:17:53,950
You would call upon them to fight?

688
01:17:53,950 --> 01:17:55,660
They believe in nothing.

689
01:17:55,660 --> 01:17:57,960
They answer to no one.

690
01:17:57,960 --> 01:18:01,560
They will answer to the king of Gondor.

691
01:18:08,170 --> 01:18:13,830
Anduril, the Flame of the West, forged from the shards of Narsil.

692
01:18:27,650 --> 01:18:32,550
Sauron will not have forgotten the Sword of Elendil.

693
01:18:46,090 --> 01:18:51,010
The blade that was broken shall return to Minas Tirith.

694
01:18:51,010 --> 01:18:53,600
The man who can wield the power of this sword...

695
01:18:53,600 --> 01:18:58,000
can summon to him an army more deadly than any that walks this earth.

696
01:18:59,350 --> 01:19:01,650
Put aside the Ranger.

697
01:19:01,650 --> 01:19:05,150
Become who you were born to be.

698
01:19:05,150 --> 01:19:07,670
Take the Dimholt road.

699
01:19:33,220 --> 01:19:35,310
Why are you doing this?

700
01:19:35,310 --> 01:19:39,040
The war lies to the east. You cannot leave on the eve of battle.

701
01:19:40,940 --> 01:19:43,540
You cannot abandon the men.

702
01:19:44,320 --> 01:19:46,070
Eowyn....

703
01:19:46,070 --> 01:19:48,800
We need you here.

704
01:19:49,400 --> 01:19:51,800
Why have you come?

705
01:19:52,950 --> 01:19:55,430
Do you not know?

706
01:20:04,250 --> 01:20:07,740
It is but a shadow and a thought that you love.

707
01:20:11,140 --> 01:20:14,080
I cannot give you what you seek.

708
01:20:33,910 --> 01:20:36,370
Just where do you think you're off to?

709
01:20:36,370 --> 01:20:37,870
Not this time.

710
01:20:37,870 --> 01:20:40,600
This time you must stay, Gimli.

711
01:20:42,790 --> 01:20:45,800
Have you learned nothing of the stubbornness of Dwarves?

712
01:20:45,800 --> 01:20:49,950
You might as well accept it. We're going with you, laddie.

713
01:21:11,780 --> 01:21:14,280
-What's happening?  -Where is he going?

714
01:21:14,280 --> 01:21:16,640
Where's he going?

715
01:21:18,750 --> 01:21:21,310
I don't understand.

716
01:21:25,170 --> 01:21:27,420
Lord Aragorn!

717
01:21:27,420 --> 01:21:30,660
Why does he leave on the eve of battle?

718
01:21:31,340 --> 01:21:33,950
He leaves because there is no hope.

719
01:21:34,060 --> 01:21:36,350
He leaves because he must.

720
01:21:36,350 --> 01:21:38,270
Too few have come.

721
01:21:38,270 --> 01:21:40,920
We cannot defeat the armies of Mordor.

722
01:21:42,940 --> 01:21:45,030
No...

723
01:21:45,030 --> 01:21:46,800
...we cannot.

724
01:21:49,150 --> 01:21:53,470
But we will meet them in battle nonetheless.

725
01:22:07,380 --> 01:22:09,610
I have left instruction.

726
01:22:11,760 --> 01:22:15,540
The people are to follow your rule in my stead.

727
01:22:21,600 --> 01:22:24,380
Take up my seat in the Golden Hall.

728
01:22:25,110 --> 01:22:28,110
Long may you defend Edoras...

729
01:22:28,110 --> 01:22:30,970
if the battle goes ill.

730
01:22:31,570 --> 01:22:35,470
What other duty would you have me do, my lord?

731
01:22:37,200 --> 01:22:39,640
Duty?

732
01:22:41,290 --> 01:22:43,190
No.

733
01:22:50,930 --> 01:22:53,580
I would have you smile again...

734
01:22:56,520 --> 01:23:02,000
not grieve for those whose time has come.

735
01:23:06,320 --> 01:23:10,380
You shall live to see these days renewed...

736
01:23:14,200 --> 01:23:17,430
and no more despair.

737
01:23:23,130 --> 01:23:27,010
What kind of army would linger in such a place?

738
01:23:27,010 --> 01:23:29,360
One that is cursed.

739
01:23:30,800 --> 01:23:33,810
Long ago, the Men of the Mountains swore an oath...

740
01:23:33,810 --> 01:23:37,080
to the last king of Gondor...

741
01:23:37,140 --> 01:23:38,890
to come to his aid...

742
01:23:38,890 --> 01:23:41,100
to fight.

743
01:23:41,100 --> 01:23:43,790
But when the time came...

744
01:23:43,900 --> 01:23:46,650
when Gondor's need was dire...

745
01:23:46,650 --> 01:23:48,740
they fled...

746
01:23:48,740 --> 01:23:52,640
vanishing into the darkness of the mountain.

747
01:23:53,160 --> 01:23:55,970
And so lsildur cursed them...

748
01:23:57,000 --> 01:24:01,400
never to rest until they had fulfilled their pledge.

749
01:24:15,180 --> 01:24:19,000
The very warmth of my blood seems stole away.

750
01:24:24,020 --> 01:24:26,460
The way is shut.

751
01:24:26,690 --> 01:24:29,220
It was made by those who are dead.

752
01:24:29,320 --> 01:24:32,050
And the Dead keep it.

753
01:24:32,070 --> 01:24:34,140
The way is shut.

754
01:24:45,000 --> 01:24:46,990
Brego!

755
01:24:49,970 --> 01:24:53,200
I do not fear death.

756
01:25:04,980 --> 01:25:07,570
this is a thing unheard-of.

757
01:25:07,570 --> 01:25:12,410
An Elf will go underground where a Dwarf dare not?

758
01:25:12,410 --> 01:25:13,910
Oh.

759
01:25:13,910 --> 01:25:17,270
Oh, I'd never hear the end of it.

760
01:25:31,760 --> 01:25:34,180
We must ride light and swift.

761
01:25:34,180 --> 01:25:36,100
It is a long road ahead.

762
01:25:36,100 --> 01:25:39,710
And man and beast must reach the end with the strength to fight.

763
01:25:44,690 --> 01:25:48,070
Little Hobbits do not belong in war, Master Meriadoc.

764
01:25:48,070 --> 01:25:50,200
All my friends have gone to battle.

765
01:25:50,200 --> 01:25:52,280
I would be ashamed to be left behind.

766
01:25:52,280 --> 01:25:54,540
It is a three-day gallop to Minas Tirith.

767
01:25:54,540 --> 01:25:57,430
And none of my riders can bear you as a burden.

768
01:25:57,960 --> 01:26:00,540
I want to fight.

769
01:26:00,540 --> 01:26:03,060
I will say no more.

770
01:26:19,350 --> 01:26:21,830
Ride with me.

771
01:26:22,810 --> 01:26:24,360
My lady.

772
01:26:24,360 --> 01:26:26,900
Form up! Move out!

773
01:26:26,900 --> 01:26:30,640
Form up! Move out!

774
01:26:33,200 --> 01:26:34,620
Ride!

775
01:26:34,620 --> 01:26:38,060
Ride now to Gondor!

776
01:27:25,420 --> 01:27:31,070
Who enters my domain?

777
01:27:34,310 --> 01:27:37,040
One who will have your allegiance.

778
01:27:39,480 --> 01:27:45,190
The Dead do not suffer the living to pass.

779
01:27:45,190 --> 01:27:48,340
You will suffer me.

780
01:28:11,340 --> 01:28:15,240
The way is shut.

781
01:28:15,930 --> 01:28:20,770
It was made by those who are dead.

782
01:28:20,770 --> 01:28:25,420
And the Dead keep it.

783
01:28:34,030 --> 01:28:37,640
The way is shut.

784
01:28:38,910 --> 01:28:42,020
Now you must die.

785
01:28:45,380 --> 01:28:48,590
I summon you to fulfill your oath.

786
01:28:48,590 --> 01:28:54,030
None but the king of Gondor may command me.

787
01:28:59,140 --> 01:29:01,790
That line was broken.

788
01:29:03,940 --> 01:29:06,630
It has been remade.

789
01:29:14,030 --> 01:29:15,740
Fight for us...

790
01:29:15,740 --> 01:29:18,810
and regain your honor.

791
01:29:22,500 --> 01:29:24,320
What say you?

792
01:29:36,020 --> 01:29:38,080
What say you?

793
01:29:38,350 --> 01:29:40,270
You waste your time, Aragorn.

794
01:29:40,270 --> 01:29:43,980
They had no honor in life, they have none now in death.

795
01:29:43,980 --> 01:29:46,960
I am Isildur's heir.

796
01:29:47,030 --> 01:29:49,510
Fight for me...

797
01:29:49,530 --> 01:29:53,680
and I will hold your oaths fulfilled.

798
01:29:57,040 --> 01:29:59,560
What say you?

799
01:30:09,470 --> 01:30:12,530
Open the gate! Quick!

800
01:30:43,090 --> 01:30:45,570
Quick! Hurry!

801
01:30:49,630 --> 01:30:51,780
Faramir!

802
01:30:52,260 --> 01:30:56,040
Say not that he has fallen.

803
01:30:56,680 --> 01:30:58,640
They were outnumbered.

804
01:30:58,640 --> 01:31:00,710
None survived.

805
01:31:00,940 --> 01:31:03,460
Fear.

806
01:31:03,480 --> 01:31:07,210
The city is rank with it.

807
01:31:09,030 --> 01:31:11,740
Let us ease their pain.

808
01:31:11,740 --> 01:31:13,660
Release the prisoners.

809
01:31:13,660 --> 01:31:16,140
Catapults!

810
01:31:28,970 --> 01:31:32,950
My sons are spent.

811
01:31:33,470 --> 01:31:36,910
My line has ended.

812
01:31:39,230 --> 01:31:40,810
He's alive!

813
01:31:40,810 --> 01:31:44,150
The House of Stewards has failed.

814
01:31:44,150 --> 01:31:46,130
He needs medicine, my lord.

815
01:31:46,650 --> 01:31:49,800
My line has ended!

816
01:31:50,820 --> 01:31:53,350
My lord!

817
01:32:06,340 --> 01:32:08,700
Rohan...

818
01:32:08,930 --> 01:32:11,820
...has deserted us.

819
01:32:25,780 --> 01:32:29,510
Theoden's betrayed me.

820
01:32:40,040 --> 01:32:42,480
Abandon your posts!

821
01:32:43,000 --> 01:32:47,440
Flee! Flee for your lives!

822
01:32:57,060 --> 01:32:59,120
Prepare for battle!

823
01:32:59,140 --> 01:33:02,840
Hurry, men! to the wall! Defend the wall!

824
01:33:03,480 --> 01:33:05,960
Over here!

825
01:33:06,190 --> 01:33:09,090
Return to your posts!

826
01:33:19,370 --> 01:33:22,520
Send these foul beasts into the abyss.

827
01:33:32,180 --> 01:33:34,160
Stay where you are.

828
01:33:50,610 --> 01:33:52,200
We need more rubble!

829
01:33:52,200 --> 01:33:54,240
Watch out!

830
01:33:54,240 --> 01:33:57,310
Down to the lower level. Quick!

831
01:33:58,660 --> 01:34:00,730
Double up, men!

832
01:35:03,020 --> 01:35:06,510
Hold them back! Do not give in to fear.

833
01:35:06,530 --> 01:35:10,510
Stand to your posts! Fight!

834
01:35:50,700 --> 01:35:52,490
Not to the towers!

835
01:35:52,490 --> 01:35:56,020
Aim for the trolls! Kill the trolls!

836
01:35:56,250 --> 01:35:58,560
Bring them down!

837
01:36:04,300 --> 01:36:06,510
Fight them back!

838
01:36:06,510 --> 01:36:09,030
Peregrin Took!

839
01:36:09,430 --> 01:36:13,080
-Go back to the Citadel  -They'd called us out to fight.

840
01:36:25,610 --> 01:36:28,510
This is no place for a Hobbit.

841
01:36:53,720 --> 01:36:55,700
Guard of the Citadel, indeed.

842
01:36:55,810 --> 01:36:59,620
Now, back, up the hill. Quickly. Quick!

843
01:37:05,400 --> 01:37:11,110
Grond! Grond! Grond! Grond!

844
01:37:11,110 --> 01:37:15,080
Grond! Grond! Grond!

845
01:37:15,080 --> 01:37:23,900
Grond! Grond! Grond! Grond! Grond!

846
01:37:31,590 --> 01:37:34,240
In there.

847
01:37:35,390 --> 01:37:37,790
What is this place?

848
01:37:41,520 --> 01:37:45,590
Master must go inside the tunnel.

849
01:37:46,440 --> 01:37:50,970
Now that I'm here, I don't think I want to.

850
01:37:52,530 --> 01:37:55,310
It's the only way.

851
01:37:57,040 --> 01:37:59,690
Go in...

852
01:37:59,710 --> 01:38:02,440
...or go back.

853
01:38:04,590 --> 01:38:07,900
I can't go back.

854
01:38:19,560 --> 01:38:22,270
-What's that smell  -Orcses' filth.

855
01:38:22,270 --> 01:38:26,210
Orcses come in here sometimes.

856
01:38:30,660 --> 01:38:33,050
Hurry.

857
01:38:37,410 --> 01:38:39,890
This way.

858
01:38:42,040 --> 01:38:44,520
Smeagol?

859
01:38:44,800 --> 01:38:47,650
Over here.

860
01:38:55,430 --> 01:38:58,770
It's sticky. What is it?

861
01:38:58,770 --> 01:39:01,270
You'll see.

862
01:39:01,270 --> 01:39:03,520
yes.

863
01:39:03,520 --> 01:39:07,420
You will see.

864
01:39:15,790 --> 01:39:17,980
Smeagol?

865
01:39:18,790 --> 01:39:20,560
Smeagol!

866
01:39:22,630 --> 01:39:25,190
Smeagol!

867
01:39:33,970 --> 01:39:36,410
Sam.

868
01:41:15,950 --> 01:41:18,250
And you, Frodo Baggins...

869
01:41:18,250 --> 01:41:24,150
...I give you the light of Earendil, our most beloved star.

870
01:41:24,420 --> 01:41:27,880
May it be a light for you in dark places...

871
01:41:27,880 --> 01:41:32,240
when all other lights go out.

872
01:42:47,760 --> 01:42:51,220
Naughty little fly

873
01:42:51,220 --> 01:42:54,950
Why does he cry?

874
01:42:55,010 --> 01:42:58,520
Caught in a web

875
01:42:58,520 --> 01:43:03,960
Soon you'll be...Eaten.

876
01:43:40,600 --> 01:43:43,480
Got away, did it, precious?

877
01:43:43,480 --> 01:43:45,780
Not this time.

878
01:43:45,780 --> 01:43:49,380
-Not this time  -No!

879
01:43:55,700 --> 01:43:59,500
It wasn't us. It wasn't us!

880
01:43:59,500 --> 01:44:02,290
Smeagol wouldn't hurt master.

881
01:44:02,290 --> 01:44:04,380
We promised.

882
01:44:04,380 --> 01:44:07,050
You must believe us.

883
01:44:07,050 --> 01:44:08,930
It was the precious.

884
01:44:08,930 --> 01:44:14,240
The precious made us do it.

885
01:44:30,820 --> 01:44:34,260
I have to destroy it, Smeagol.

886
01:44:42,750 --> 01:44:46,610
I have to destroy it for both our sakes.

887
01:44:55,600 --> 01:44:58,080
No!

888
01:45:20,830 --> 01:45:23,770
I'm so sorry, Sam.

889
01:45:27,720 --> 01:45:30,820
I'm so sorry.

890
01:45:56,040 --> 01:46:01,400
This task was appointed to you, Frodo of the Shire.

891
01:46:02,040 --> 01:46:04,940
If you do not find a way...

892
01:46:05,710 --> 01:46:07,440
no one will.

893
01:46:54,890 --> 01:46:56,980
Back to the gate!

894
01:46:56,980 --> 01:46:59,710
Hurry!

895
01:47:22,420 --> 01:47:25,940
No tomb for Denethor and Faramir.

896
01:47:26,550 --> 01:47:32,760
No long, slow sleep of death embalmed.

897
01:47:32,760 --> 01:47:38,460
We shall burn, like the heathen kings of old.

898
01:47:41,560 --> 01:47:43,920
Bring wood and oil.

899
01:47:46,150 --> 01:47:47,740
Steady.

900
01:47:47,740 --> 01:47:50,300
Steady.

901
01:48:04,170 --> 01:48:07,010
You are soldiers of Gondor.

902
01:48:07,010 --> 01:48:11,950
No matter what comes through that gate, you will stand your ground.

903
01:48:21,020 --> 01:48:23,000
Volley!

904
01:48:23,230 --> 01:48:25,670
Fire!

905
01:50:18,310 --> 01:50:20,830
Let him go, you filth.

906
01:50:22,230 --> 01:50:24,460
Let him go!

907
01:50:25,150 --> 01:50:27,840
You will not touch him again.

908
01:50:30,490 --> 01:50:32,850
Come on and finish it.

909
01:52:22,110 --> 01:52:24,210
Back!

910
01:52:34,490 --> 01:52:36,310
Mr. Frodo.

911
01:52:45,340 --> 01:52:47,510
Oh, no.

912
01:52:47,510 --> 01:52:49,800
Frodo.

913
01:52:49,800 --> 01:52:52,160
Mr. Frodo.

914
01:52:56,220 --> 01:52:58,120
Wake up.

915
01:53:01,440 --> 01:53:04,300
Don't leave me here alone.

916
01:53:05,320 --> 01:53:08,260
Don't go where I can't follow.

917
01:53:12,030 --> 01:53:13,970
Wake up.

918
01:53:20,120 --> 01:53:22,810
Not asleep.

919
01:53:24,460 --> 01:53:26,860
Dead.

920
01:53:56,200 --> 01:53:58,060
What's this?

921
01:53:58,710 --> 01:54:02,020
Looks like old Shelob's been having a bit of fun.

922
01:54:03,460 --> 01:54:06,210
Killed another one, has she?

923
01:54:06,210 --> 01:54:08,700
No.

924
01:54:10,890 --> 01:54:13,220
This fellow ain't dead.

925
01:54:13,220 --> 01:54:15,640
Not dead?

926
01:54:15,640 --> 01:54:21,770
She jabs him with her stinger, and he goes as limp as a boned fish.

927
01:54:21,770 --> 01:54:24,900
Then she has her way with them.

928
01:54:24,900 --> 01:54:27,070
That's how she likes to feed.

929
01:54:27,070 --> 01:54:29,400
Fresh blood.

930
01:54:29,400 --> 01:54:32,220
Get him to the tower!

931
01:54:35,160 --> 01:54:37,080
Samwise, you fool.

932
01:54:37,080 --> 01:54:40,080
This scum will be awake in a couple of hours.

933
01:54:40,080 --> 01:54:43,060
Then he'll wish he'd never been born.

934
01:55:06,820 --> 01:55:10,590
The house of his spirit crumbles.

935
01:55:11,110 --> 01:55:13,100
He is burning.

936
01:55:13,740 --> 01:55:15,450
Already burning.

937
01:55:15,450 --> 01:55:17,910
He's not dead.

938
01:55:17,910 --> 01:55:20,100
He's not dead!

939
01:55:21,790 --> 01:55:23,710
No! No!

940
01:55:23,710 --> 01:55:26,260
No! No!

941
01:55:26,260 --> 01:55:28,630
He's not dead!

942
01:55:28,630 --> 01:55:32,260
-Farewell, Peregrin, son of Paladin.  -No! No! No!

943
01:55:32,260 --> 01:55:36,080
I release you from my service.

944
01:55:36,890 --> 01:55:41,750
Go now and die in what way seems best to you.

945
01:55:43,440 --> 01:55:46,300
Pour oil on the wood!

946
01:55:47,490 --> 01:55:49,990
Come on! Move your feet!

947
01:55:49,990 --> 01:55:53,330
-Hurry along there! Hurry along  -Gandalf!

948
01:55:53,330 --> 01:55:55,270
Where is Gandalf?

949
01:55:55,870 --> 01:55:57,810
Gandalf!

950
01:56:02,670 --> 01:56:04,320
Retreat!

951
01:56:05,960 --> 01:56:07,840
The city is breached!

952
01:56:07,840 --> 01:56:11,370
Fall back to the second level!

953
01:56:14,640 --> 01:56:16,560
Get the women and children out!

954
01:56:16,560 --> 01:56:18,520
Get them out!

955
01:56:18,520 --> 01:56:20,190
Retreat!

956
01:56:20,190 --> 01:56:22,310
Come on. Come on.

957
01:56:22,310 --> 01:56:27,050
Move into the city. Kill all in your path.

958
01:56:34,540 --> 01:56:37,520
Take them down!

959
01:56:57,520 --> 01:57:00,560
Fight. Fight to the last man!

960
01:57:00,560 --> 01:57:02,380
Fight for your lives!

961
01:57:51,450 --> 01:57:53,080
Courage, Merry.

962
01:57:53,080 --> 01:57:55,930
Courage for our friends.

963
01:57:58,960 --> 01:58:02,250
Form ranks, you maggots. Form ranks!

964
01:58:02,250 --> 01:58:05,980
Pikes in front. Archers behind.

965
01:58:13,600 --> 01:58:16,890
Eomer,take your eored the left flank.

966
01:58:16,890 --> 01:58:18,310
Flank ready.

967
01:58:18,310 --> 01:58:21,350
Gamling, follow the king's banner down the center.

968
01:58:21,350 --> 01:58:25,280
Grimbold, take your company right after you pass the wall.

969
01:58:25,280 --> 01:58:28,150
Forth, and fear no darkness!

970
01:58:28,150 --> 01:58:32,280
Arise, arise, Riders of Theoden!

971
01:58:32,280 --> 01:58:37,660
Spears shall be shaken, shields shall be splintered...

972
01:58:37,660 --> 01:58:41,500
a sword-day, a red day...

973
01:58:41,500 --> 01:58:45,610
Here the sun rises!

974
01:58:52,850 --> 01:58:57,710
Whatever happens, stay with me. I'll look after you.

975
01:59:03,520 --> 01:59:06,130
Ride now!

976
01:59:07,110 --> 01:59:09,760
Ride now!

977
01:59:09,860 --> 01:59:12,780
Ride! Ride for ruin...

978
01:59:12,780 --> 01:59:16,060
and the world's ending!

979
01:59:17,500 --> 01:59:19,330
Death!

980
01:59:19,330 --> 01:59:22,380
Death!

981
01:59:22,380 --> 01:59:26,050
-Death!  -Death!

982
01:59:26,050 --> 01:59:28,150
-Death!  -Death!

983
01:59:28,380 --> 01:59:32,320
-Death!  -Death!

984
01:59:36,890 --> 01:59:39,870
Forth Eorlingas!

985
02:00:22,270 --> 02:00:24,590
Fire!

986
02:00:27,860 --> 02:00:29,590
Death!

987
02:00:33,280 --> 02:00:34,990
Charge!

988
02:00:34,990 --> 02:00:37,100
Fire at will!

989
02:01:03,480 --> 02:01:05,250
Gandalf!

990
02:01:07,280 --> 02:01:11,320
Gandalf! Denethor has lost his mind!

991
02:01:11,320 --> 02:01:13,740
He's burning Faramir alive!

992
02:01:13,740 --> 02:01:16,020
Up! Quickly!

993
02:01:46,320 --> 02:01:50,090
Set a fire in our flesh.

994
02:02:07,210 --> 02:02:09,530
Stay this madness!

995
02:02:43,340 --> 02:02:45,210
No!

996
02:02:45,210 --> 02:02:48,090
You will not take my son from me!

997
02:02:48,090 --> 02:02:50,910
No! No!

998
02:03:01,350 --> 02:03:03,540
Faramir.

999
02:03:16,580 --> 02:03:21,060
So passes Denethor, son of Ecthelion.

1000
02:03:48,070 --> 02:03:50,340
Drive them to the river!

1001
02:03:52,620 --> 02:03:55,100
Make safe the city!

1002
02:04:34,620 --> 02:04:37,060
Re-form the line!

1003
02:04:37,710 --> 02:04:40,190
Re-form the line!

1004
02:04:46,670 --> 02:04:49,820
Sound the charge! Take them head-on!

1005
02:04:49,880 --> 02:04:52,570
Charge!

1006
02:05:58,250 --> 02:06:00,150
Cut him down!

1007
02:06:01,420 --> 02:06:03,820
Follow me!

1008
02:06:26,320 --> 02:06:29,430
Take the reins. Pull him left!

1009
02:06:31,320 --> 02:06:33,140
Left!

1010
02:06:50,010 --> 02:06:52,200
Aim for their heads!

1011
02:06:57,680 --> 02:07:01,500
Bring it down! Bring it down! Bring it down!

1012
02:07:14,830 --> 02:07:16,850
Merry!

1013
02:07:38,060 --> 02:07:40,580
I didn't think it would end this way.

1014
02:07:41,400 --> 02:07:43,290
End?

1015
02:07:44,020 --> 02:07:46,670
No, the journey doesn't end here.

1016
02:07:48,650 --> 02:07:52,300
Death is just another path...

1017
02:07:52,370 --> 02:07:54,560
one that we all must take.

1018
02:07:55,290 --> 02:07:58,910
The grey rain curtain of this world rolls back...

1019
02:07:58,910 --> 02:08:03,060
...and all turns to silver glass.

1020
02:08:04,710 --> 02:08:07,190
And then you see it.

1021
02:08:08,590 --> 02:08:11,490
What, Gandalf?

1022
02:08:12,100 --> 02:08:13,950
See what?

1023
02:08:14,680 --> 02:08:17,410
White shores...

1024
02:08:18,560 --> 02:08:21,500
and beyond.

1025
02:08:22,440 --> 02:08:24,750
A far green country...

1026
02:08:24,940 --> 02:08:28,380
under a swift sunrise.

1027
02:08:31,910 --> 02:08:33,580
Well...

1028
02:08:33,580 --> 02:08:35,450
...that isn't so bad.

1029
02:08:35,450 --> 02:08:37,350
No.

1030
02:08:38,870 --> 02:08:41,060
No, it isn't.

1031
02:08:56,930 --> 02:09:00,790
Rally to me! to me!

1032
02:09:21,040 --> 02:09:26,110
Feast on his flesh.

1033
02:09:29,930 --> 02:09:32,470
I will kill you if you touch him.

1034
02:09:32,470 --> 02:09:38,460
Do not come between the Nazgul and his prey.

1035
02:10:46,340 --> 02:10:49,970
Late as usual, pirate scum!

1036
02:10:49,970 --> 02:10:52,390
There's knife-work here needs doing.

1037
02:10:52,390 --> 02:10:56,120
Come on, you sea rats! Get off your ships!

1038
02:11:11,070 --> 02:11:13,370
There's plenty for the both of us.

1039
02:11:13,370 --> 02:11:15,970
May the best Dwarf win.

1040
02:11:40,020 --> 02:11:42,440
You fool.

1041
02:11:42,440 --> 02:11:46,340
No man can kill me.

1042
02:11:48,200 --> 02:11:51,890
Die now.

1043
02:12:02,040 --> 02:12:04,570
I am no man.

1044
02:12:20,650 --> 02:12:24,630
-Fifteen! Sixteen!  -Seventeen!

1045
02:12:40,290 --> 02:12:43,440
-Twenty-nine!  -Legolas!

1046
02:13:05,320 --> 02:13:08,220
Thirty-three, thirty-four.

1047
02:13:54,790 --> 02:13:57,330
That still only counts as one!

1048
02:13:57,330 --> 02:14:00,020
All right, then. Come on!

1049
02:14:43,210 --> 02:14:46,570
I know your face...

1050
02:14:47,920 --> 02:14:50,320
...Eowyn.

1051
02:14:52,350 --> 02:14:55,240
My eyes darken.

1052
02:14:55,850 --> 02:14:57,750
No.

1053
02:14:58,060 --> 02:15:00,210
No.

1054
02:15:01,810 --> 02:15:04,800
I am going to save you.

1055
02:15:05,610 --> 02:15:08,510
You already did.

1056
02:15:11,620 --> 02:15:13,760
Eowyn...

1057
02:15:14,740 --> 02:15:17,770
...my body is broken.

1058
02:15:22,290 --> 02:15:25,280
You have to let me go.

1059
02:15:30,680 --> 02:15:33,740
I go to my fathers...

1060
02:15:34,680 --> 02:15:37,980
...in whose mighty company...

1061
02:15:37,980 --> 02:15:41,830
I shall not now feel ashamed.

1062
02:15:57,910 --> 02:16:00,060
Eowyn.

1063
02:16:46,050 --> 02:16:49,030
Release us.

1064
02:16:50,430 --> 02:16:52,300
Bad idea.

1065
02:16:52,300 --> 02:16:56,310
Very handy in a tight spot, these lads, despite the fact they're dead.

1066
02:16:56,310 --> 02:16:58,830
You gave us your word.

1067
02:17:00,100 --> 02:17:02,710
I hold your oath fulfilled.

1068
02:17:03,520 --> 02:17:05,380
Go.

1069
02:17:05,730 --> 02:17:07,920
Be at peace.

1070
02:17:42,060 --> 02:17:44,090
Merry.

1071
02:17:46,320 --> 02:17:48,090
Merry, it's me.

1072
02:17:50,200 --> 02:17:52,260
It's Pippin.

1073
02:17:54,240 --> 02:17:56,660
I knew you'd find me.

1074
02:17:56,660 --> 02:17:58,430
Yes.

1075
02:18:00,330 --> 02:18:02,940
Are you going to leave me?

1076
02:18:02,960 --> 02:18:05,150
No, Merry.

1077
02:18:05,960 --> 02:18:08,700
I'm going to look after you.

1078
02:18:52,220 --> 02:18:53,810
Hands off!

1079
02:18:53,810 --> 02:18:57,230
That shiny shirt, that's mine.

1080
02:18:57,230 --> 02:19:01,880
It's going to the Great Eye, along with everything else.

1081
02:19:02,900 --> 02:19:07,260
I don't take orders from stinking Morgul rats!

1082
02:19:07,610 --> 02:19:13,300
You touch it, and I'll stick this blade in your gut.

1083
02:19:33,470 --> 02:19:35,430
The scum tried to knife me.

1084
02:19:35,430 --> 02:19:37,710
Kill him!

1085
02:20:58,430 --> 02:21:00,850
That's for Frodo!

1086
02:21:00,850 --> 02:21:03,460
And for the Shire!

1087
02:21:06,530 --> 02:21:09,180
And that's for my old Gaffer!

1088
02:21:30,590 --> 02:21:34,410
Stop your squealing, you dunghill rat.

1089
02:21:35,060 --> 02:21:40,290
I'm gonna bleed you like a stuck pig.

1090
02:21:47,110 --> 02:21:48,950
Not if I stick you first.

1091
02:21:48,950 --> 02:21:51,010
Sam!

1092
02:21:55,540 --> 02:21:57,750
Sam, I'm so sorry.

1093
02:21:57,750 --> 02:22:00,290
Sorry for everything.

1094
02:22:00,290 --> 02:22:04,090
-Let's get you out of here.  -It's too late. It's over.

1095
02:22:04,090 --> 02:22:07,530
They've taken it. Sam...

1096
02:22:07,760 --> 02:22:09,780
...they took the Ring.

1097
02:22:10,050 --> 02:22:13,240
Begging your pardon, but they haven't.

1098
02:22:24,730 --> 02:22:27,320
I thought I'd lost you.

1099
02:22:27,320 --> 02:22:29,550
So I took it.

1100
02:22:30,200 --> 02:22:32,760
Only for safekeeping.

1101
02:22:33,530 --> 02:22:35,770
Give it to me.

1102
02:22:38,830 --> 02:22:41,560
Give me the Ring, Sam.

1103
02:22:45,710 --> 02:22:47,440
Sam.

1104
02:22:48,550 --> 02:22:51,030
Give me the Ring.

1105
02:23:11,240 --> 02:23:13,010
You must understand.

1106
02:23:15,990 --> 02:23:18,350
The Ring is my burden.

1107
02:23:19,040 --> 02:23:21,690
It will destroy you, Sam.

1108
02:23:24,340 --> 02:23:26,860
Come on, Mr. Frodo.

1109
02:23:27,670 --> 02:23:29,470
We best find you some clothes.

1110
02:23:29,470 --> 02:23:32,990
You can't go walking through Mordor in naught but your skin.

1111
02:23:54,200 --> 02:23:56,950
We did it, Mr. Frodo.

1112
02:23:56,950 --> 02:23:59,770
We made it to Mordor.

1113
02:24:00,580 --> 02:24:02,770
There are so many of them.

1114
02:24:03,210 --> 02:24:06,320
We'll never get through unseen.

1115
02:24:10,930 --> 02:24:14,790
It's him, the Eye.

1116
02:24:21,980 --> 02:24:25,070
We have to go in there, Mr. Frodo.

1117
02:24:25,070 --> 02:24:27,630
There's nothing for it.

1118
02:24:30,070 --> 02:24:35,060
Come on. Let's just make it down the hill for starters.

1119
02:24:43,880 --> 02:24:47,650
Frodo has passed beyond my sight.

1120
02:24:48,470 --> 02:24:51,470
The darkness is deepening.

1121
02:24:51,470 --> 02:24:54,010
If Sauron had the Ring, we would know it.

1122
02:24:54,010 --> 02:24:56,580
It's only a matter of time.

1123
02:24:57,560 --> 02:25:00,460
He has suffered a defeat, yes...

1124
02:25:01,020 --> 02:25:05,690
...but behind the walls of Mordor, our enemy is regrouping.

1125
02:25:05,690 --> 02:25:07,690
Let him stay there.

1126
02:25:07,690 --> 02:25:10,530
Let him rot! Why should we care?

1127
02:25:10,530 --> 02:25:16,220
Because 1 0,000 Orcs now stand between Frodo and Mount Doom.

1128
02:25:22,460 --> 02:25:25,440
I've sent him to his death.

1129
02:25:26,510 --> 02:25:28,280
No.

1130
02:25:28,300 --> 02:25:31,050
There is still hope for Frodo.

1131
02:25:31,050 --> 02:25:35,700
He needs time and safe passage across the plains of Gorgoroth.

1132
02:25:36,270 --> 02:25:39,140
-We can give him that.  -How?

1133
02:25:39,140 --> 02:25:42,060
Draw out Sauron's armies.

1134
02:25:42,060 --> 02:25:44,400
Empty his lands.

1135
02:25:44,400 --> 02:25:47,970
Then we gather our full strength and march on the Black Gate.

1136
02:25:48,110 --> 02:25:51,280
We cannot achieve victory through strength of arms.

1137
02:25:51,280 --> 02:25:53,080
Not for ourselves.

1138
02:25:53,080 --> 02:25:59,140
But we can give Frodo his chance if we keep Sauron's Eye fixed upon us.

1139
02:26:00,460 --> 02:26:04,770
Keep him blind to all else that moves.

1140
02:26:05,000 --> 02:26:06,740
A diversion.

1141
02:26:07,010 --> 02:26:09,950
Sauron will suspect a trap.

1142
02:26:10,180 --> 02:26:12,430
He will not take the bait.

1143
02:26:12,430 --> 02:26:14,180
Certainty of death...

1144
02:26:14,180 --> 02:26:17,330
small chance of success...

1145
02:26:17,850 --> 02:26:19,960
what are we waiting for?

1146
02:26:38,040 --> 02:26:41,560
To the Gate, you slugs!

1147
02:26:41,960 --> 02:26:46,030
Move it! to the Gate!

1148
02:26:51,550 --> 02:26:53,720
Look, the Orcs...

1149
02:26:53,720 --> 02:26:56,250
they're moving off.

1150
02:26:56,890 --> 02:26:59,060
You see, Mr. Frodo...

1151
02:26:59,060 --> 02:27:01,790
some luck at last.

1152
02:27:56,250 --> 02:27:58,370
Take mine.

1153
02:27:58,370 --> 02:28:00,980
There's a few drops left.

1154
02:28:15,720 --> 02:28:18,790
There will be none left for the return journey.

1155
02:28:19,190 --> 02:28:22,920
I don't think there will be a return journey, Mr. Frodo.

1156
02:29:15,290 --> 02:29:17,980
Frodo, get down!

1157
02:29:19,210 --> 02:29:21,600
Hide!

1158
02:29:31,220 --> 02:29:33,780
Frodo!

1159
02:29:39,100 --> 02:29:41,080
Where are they?

1160
02:30:16,600 --> 02:30:20,210
Let the Lord of the Black Land come forth!

1161
02:30:20,600 --> 02:30:23,960
Let justice be done upon him!

1162
02:30:55,850 --> 02:30:57,980
Fall back.

1163
02:30:57,980 --> 02:31:00,500
Fall back!

1164
02:31:12,200 --> 02:31:14,760
It's gone, Mr. Frodo.

1165
02:31:16,160 --> 02:31:19,920
The light's passed on, away towards the north.

1166
02:31:19,920 --> 02:31:22,230
Something's drawn its gaze.

1167
02:31:39,230 --> 02:31:42,500
Hold your ground! Hold your ground.

1168
02:31:44,070 --> 02:31:48,590
Sons of Gondor, of Rohan, my brothers!

1169
02:31:50,950 --> 02:31:53,200
I see in your eyes...

1170
02:31:53,200 --> 02:31:57,770
the same fear that would take the heart of me.

1171
02:31:59,210 --> 02:32:02,750
A day may come when the courage of Men fails...

1172
02:32:02,750 --> 02:32:06,760
when we forsake our friends and break all bonds of fellowship.

1173
02:32:06,760 --> 02:32:09,720
But it is not this day.

1174
02:32:09,720 --> 02:32:12,930
An hour of wolves and shattered shields...

1175
02:32:12,930 --> 02:32:15,970
when the age of Men comes crashing down.

1176
02:32:15,970 --> 02:32:18,600
But it is not this day.

1177
02:32:18,600 --> 02:32:20,790
This day we fight!

1178
02:32:22,110 --> 02:32:26,570
By all that you hold dear on this good earth...

1179
02:32:26,570 --> 02:32:31,340
I bid you stand, Men of the West!

1180
02:33:59,330 --> 02:34:03,340
Never thought I'd die fighting side by side with an Elf.

1181
02:34:03,340 --> 02:34:06,190
What about side by side with a friend?

1182
02:34:09,180 --> 02:34:11,490
Aye.

1183
02:34:11,800 --> 02:34:14,080
I could do that.

1184
02:34:43,880 --> 02:34:46,490
Do you remember the Shire, Mr. Frodo?

1185
02:34:48,930 --> 02:34:51,700
It'll be spring soon.

1186
02:34:52,010 --> 02:34:54,890
And the orchards will be in blossom.

1187
02:34:54,890 --> 02:34:59,040
And the birds will be nesting in the hazel thicket.

1188
02:34:59,890 --> 02:35:04,420
And they'll be sowing the summer barley in the lower fields...

1189
02:35:04,940 --> 02:35:09,840
and eating the first of the strawberries with cream.

1190
02:35:11,240 --> 02:35:14,260
Do you remember the taste of strawberries?

1191
02:35:15,370 --> 02:35:17,250
No, Sam.

1192
02:35:17,250 --> 02:35:20,690
I can't recall the taste of food...

1193
02:35:21,290 --> 02:35:24,750
nor the sound of water...

1194
02:35:24,750 --> 02:35:28,900
...nor the touch of grass.

1195
02:35:29,300 --> 02:35:31,370
I'm...

1196
02:35:31,760 --> 02:35:33,620
naked in the dark.

1197
02:35:34,760 --> 02:35:37,270
There's...There's nothing.

1198
02:35:37,270 --> 02:35:42,460
No veil between me and the wheel of fire.

1199
02:35:43,190 --> 02:35:45,570
I can see him...

1200
02:35:45,570 --> 02:35:47,720
...with my waking eyes.

1201
02:35:48,280 --> 02:35:51,260
Then let us be rid of it...

1202
02:35:51,280 --> 02:35:54,100
once and for all.

1203
02:35:54,280 --> 02:35:56,500
Come on, Mr. Frodo.

1204
02:35:56,500 --> 02:35:59,580
I can't carry it for you...

1205
02:35:59,580 --> 02:36:02,110
...but I can carry you.

1206
02:36:02,130 --> 02:36:04,440
Come on!

1207
02:36:34,330 --> 02:36:37,770
Aragorn.

1208
02:36:48,840 --> 02:36:51,950
Elessar.

1209
02:37:03,400 --> 02:37:06,380
For Frodo.

1210
02:37:40,770 --> 02:37:42,790
Look, Mr. Frodo.

1211
02:37:42,980 --> 02:37:45,710
A doorway.

1212
02:37:45,780 --> 02:37:47,970
We're almost there.

1213
02:37:49,780 --> 02:37:54,260
Clever Hobbits to climb so high!

1214
02:38:53,390 --> 02:38:55,790
Frodo!

1215
02:39:22,330 --> 02:39:24,650
Eagles.

1216
02:39:25,500 --> 02:39:27,530
The eagles are coming!

1217
02:39:49,860 --> 02:39:52,260
Frodo!

1218
02:39:57,000 --> 02:39:58,810
I'm here, Sam.

1219
02:40:05,760 --> 02:40:07,860
Destroy it!

1220
02:40:17,930 --> 02:40:21,400
Go on! Now!

1221
02:40:21,400 --> 02:40:24,460
Throw it in the fire!

1222
02:40:37,330 --> 02:40:40,520
What are you waiting for?

1223
02:40:41,880 --> 02:40:44,730
Just let it go!

1224
02:41:17,450 --> 02:41:20,230
The Ring is mine.

1225
02:41:23,250 --> 02:41:25,420
No.

1226
02:41:25,420 --> 02:41:27,240
No.

1227
02:41:35,140 --> 02:41:38,290
No!

1228
02:43:22,250 --> 02:43:24,610
Yes!

1229
02:43:25,300 --> 02:43:27,530
Yes!

1230
02:43:28,130 --> 02:43:31,180
Precious! Precious!

1231
02:43:31,180 --> 02:43:34,870
Precious! Precious!

1232
02:44:27,280 --> 02:44:29,630
Give me your hand!

1233
02:44:37,450 --> 02:44:40,400
Take my hand!

1234
02:44:42,540 --> 02:44:44,360
No!

1235
02:44:51,140 --> 02:44:53,620
Don't you let go.

1236
02:44:57,680 --> 02:44:59,790
Don't let go.

1237
02:45:00,850 --> 02:45:02,880
Reach!

1238
02:46:31,530 --> 02:46:34,930
Frodo!

1239
02:46:34,950 --> 02:46:38,520
Frodo!

1240
02:47:59,120 --> 02:48:01,690
It's gone.

1241
02:48:05,420 --> 02:48:07,880
It's done.

1242
02:48:07,880 --> 02:48:10,410
Yes, Mr. Frodo.

1243
02:48:11,300 --> 02:48:14,240
It's over now.

1244
02:48:39,120 --> 02:48:42,230
I can see the Shire.

1245
02:48:43,920 --> 02:48:46,780
The Brandywine River.

1246
02:48:48,420 --> 02:48:50,910
Bag End.

1247
02:48:52,760 --> 02:48:55,890
Gandalf's fireworks.

1248
02:48:55,890 --> 02:49:00,170
The lights in the Party Tree.

1249
02:49:01,100 --> 02:49:04,750
Rosie Cotton dancing.

1250
02:49:05,400 --> 02:49:08,590
She had ribbons in her hair.

1251
02:49:11,030 --> 02:49:14,470
If ever I was to marry someone...

1252
02:49:14,910 --> 02:49:17,640
...it would've been her.

1253
02:49:18,620 --> 02:49:21,150
It would've been her.

1254
02:49:32,510 --> 02:49:36,540
I'm glad to be with you, Samwise Gamgee...

1255
02:49:40,310 --> 02:49:43,750
...here at the end of all things.

1256
02:51:32,930 --> 02:51:35,450
Gandalf?

1257
02:51:54,620 --> 02:51:57,100
Frodo!

1258
02:52:16,390 --> 02:52:18,750
Gimli!

1259
02:54:01,210 --> 02:54:05,480
Now come the days of the king.

1260
02:54:09,970 --> 02:54:12,780
May they be blessed.

1261
02:54:32,570 --> 02:54:35,410
This day does not belong to one man...

1262
02:54:35,410 --> 02:54:37,770
but to all.

1263
02:54:38,960 --> 02:54:42,040
Let us together rebuild this world...

1264
02:54:42,040 --> 02:54:46,780
that we may share in the days of peace.

1265
02:57:20,790 --> 02:57:23,400
My friends...

1266
02:57:28,130 --> 02:57:31,320
you bow to no one.

1267
02:58:15,010 --> 02:58:17,310
And thus it was.

1268
02:58:17,310 --> 02:58:21,100
A Fourth Age of Middle-earth began.

1269
02:58:21,100 --> 02:58:23,820
And the Fellowship of the Ring...

1270
02:58:23,820 --> 02:58:28,490
though eternally bound by friendship and love...

1271
02:58:28,490 --> 02:58:31,430
was ended.

1272
02:58:35,910 --> 02:58:40,880
Thirteen months to the day since Gandalf sent us on our long journey

1273
02:58:40,880 --> 02:58:45,610
we found ourselves looking upon a familiar sight.

1274
02:58:47,630 --> 02:58:50,860
We were home.

1275
02:58:56,890 --> 02:58:59,290
Hi.

1276
02:59:15,950 --> 02:59:18,690
Hey, watch the pumpkin.

1277
03:00:06,260 --> 03:00:07,970
Rosie, Rosie.

1278
03:00:07,970 --> 03:00:10,490
Good night, lads.

1279
03:01:07,570 --> 03:01:12,100
How do you pick up the threads of an old life?

1280
03:01:12,870 --> 03:01:15,290
How do you go on...

1281
03:01:15,290 --> 03:01:21,020
when in your heart you begin to understand...

1282
03:01:21,750 --> 03:01:25,230
there is no going back?

1283
03:01:25,380 --> 03:01:29,570
There are some things that time cannot mend...

1284
03:01:29,590 --> 03:01:33,030
some hurts that go too deep...

1285
03:01:34,260 --> 03:01:37,620
that have taken hold.

1286
03:02:15,270 --> 03:02:18,460
Mr. Frodo?

1287
03:02:20,480 --> 03:02:22,380
What is it?

1288
03:02:23,690 --> 03:02:28,130
It's been four years to the day since Weathertop, Sam.

1289
03:02:28,320 --> 03:02:31,550
It's never really healed.

1290
03:02:34,950 --> 03:02:40,770
"There and Back Again.: A Hobbit's Tale by Bilbo Baggins.

1291
03:02:41,000 --> 03:02:45,280
And The Lord of the Rings by Frodo Baggins. "

1292
03:02:45,300 --> 03:02:48,360
You finished it.

1293
03:02:50,300 --> 03:02:52,370
Not quite.

1294
03:02:52,640 --> 03:02:55,740
There's room for a little more.

1295
03:02:57,850 --> 03:03:02,230
Bilbo once told me his part in this tale would end...

1296
03:03:02,230 --> 03:03:06,050
that each of us must come and go in the telling.

1297
03:03:06,400 --> 03:03:09,740
Bilbo 's story was now over.

1298
03:03:09,740 --> 03:03:12,820
There would be no more journeys for him...

1299
03:03:12,820 --> 03:03:14,890
save one.

1300
03:03:15,120 --> 03:03:18,830
Tell me again, lad, where are we going?

1301
03:03:18,830 --> 03:03:21,000
To the harbor, Bilbo.

1302
03:03:21,000 --> 03:03:23,920
The Elves have accorded you a special honor...

1303
03:03:23,920 --> 03:03:27,070
a place on the last ship to leave Middle-earth.

1304
03:03:28,010 --> 03:03:30,780
Frodo...

1305
03:03:31,340 --> 03:03:36,370
...any chance of seeing that old Ring of mine again?

1306
03:03:36,520 --> 03:03:39,670
The one I gave you.

1307
03:03:42,360 --> 03:03:45,050
Sorry, Uncle.

1308
03:03:47,110 --> 03:03:49,860
I'm afraid I lost it.

1309
03:03:49,860 --> 03:03:52,120
Oh.

1310
03:03:52,120 --> 03:03:54,810
Pity.

1311
03:03:56,540 --> 03:04:00,900
I should like to have held it one last time.

1312
03:04:29,570 --> 03:04:35,100
Here's a sight I have never seen before.

1313
03:04:48,800 --> 03:04:52,620
The power of the Three Rings is ended.

1314
03:04:52,930 --> 03:04:55,890
The time has come...

1315
03:04:55,890 --> 03:04:59,710
for the dominion of Men.

1316
03:05:11,570 --> 03:05:13,910
I think I'm...

1317
03:05:13,910 --> 03:05:18,770
...quite ready for another adventure.

1318
03:05:49,320 --> 03:05:51,820
Farewell...

1319
03:05:51,820 --> 03:05:55,100
my brave Hobbits.

1320
03:05:56,500 --> 03:06:00,440
My work is now finished.

1321
03:06:02,170 --> 03:06:07,820
Here at last, on the shores of the sea...

1322
03:06:08,010 --> 03:06:11,320
...comes the end of our Fellowship.

1323
03:06:14,350 --> 03:06:17,410
I will not say, "Do not weep"...

1324
03:06:17,520 --> 03:06:22,080
for not all tears are an evil.

1325
03:06:38,870 --> 03:06:41,520
It is time, Frodo.

1326
03:06:46,340 --> 03:06:49,570
What does he mean?

1327
03:06:51,050 --> 03:06:54,410
We set out to save the Shire, Sam.

1328
03:06:55,520 --> 03:06:58,750
And it has been saved.

1329
03:07:01,940 --> 03:07:05,090
But not for me.

1330
03:07:05,530 --> 03:07:08,510
You don't mean that.

1331
03:07:09,200 --> 03:07:11,800
You can't leave.

1332
03:07:19,750 --> 03:07:22,980
The last pages are for you, Sam.

1333
03:10:55,560 --> 03:10:58,960
My dear Sam.:

1334
03:11:00,310 --> 03:11:03,820
You cannot always be torn in two.

1335
03:11:03,820 --> 03:11:08,470
You will have to be one and whole for many years.

1336
03:11:08,740 --> 03:11:15,350
You have so much to enjoy and to be and to do.

1337
03:11:15,450 --> 03:11:19,330
Your part in the story will go on.

1338
03:11:19,330 --> 03:11:21,980
Well...

1339
03:11:22,710 --> 03:11:25,780
...I'm back.

1340
03:13:07,320 --> 03:13:12,910
Lay down

1341
03:13:12,910 --> 03:13:19,040
Your sweet and weary head

1342
03:13:19,040 --> 03:13:23,290
Night is falling

1343
03:13:23,290 --> 03:13:28,800
You have came to journey's end

1344
03:13:28,800 --> 03:13:32,720
Sleep now

1345
03:13:32,720 --> 03:13:39,890
And dream of the ones who came before

1346
03:13:39,890 --> 03:13:44,230
They are calling

1347
03:13:44,230 --> 03:13:49,650
From across the distant shore

1348
03:13:49,650 --> 03:13:55,040
Why do you weep?

1349
03:13:55,040 --> 03:14:00,170
What are these tears upon your face?

1350
03:14:00,170 --> 03:14:05,420
Soon you will see

1351
03:14:05,420 --> 03:14:10,550
All of your fears Will pass away

1352
03:14:10,550 --> 03:14:15,810
Safe in my arms

1353
03:14:15,810 --> 03:14:20,480
You're only sleeping

1354
03:14:20,480 --> 03:14:25,650
What can you see

1355
03:14:25,650 --> 03:14:31,030
On the horizon?

1356
03:14:31,030 --> 03:14:35,740
Why do the white gulls

1357
03:14:35,740 --> 03:14:40,620
Call?

1358
03:14:40,620 --> 03:14:46,380
Across the sea

1359
03:14:46,380 --> 03:14:51,840
A pale moon rises

1360
03:14:51,840 --> 03:14:54,720
The ships have come

1361
03:14:54,720 --> 03:15:02,730
To carry you home

1362
03:15:02,730 --> 03:15:07,490
And all will turn

1363
03:15:07,490 --> 03:15:12,990
To silver glass

1364
03:15:12,990 --> 03:15:17,410
A light on the water

1365
03:15:17,410 --> 03:15:23,090
All souls pass

1366
03:15:23,090 --> 03:15:28,590
Hope fades

1367
03:15:28,590 --> 03:15:34,470
Into the world of night

1368
03:15:34,470 --> 03:15:39,100
Through shadows falling

1369
03:15:39,100 --> 03:15:44,940
Out of memory and time

1370
03:15:44,940 --> 03:15:49,490
Don 't say

1371
03:15:49,490 --> 03:15:55,330
We have come now to the end

1372
03:15:55,330 --> 03:15:59,920
White shores are calling

1373
03:15:59,920 --> 03:16:03,460
You and I will meet again

1374
03:16:03,460 --> 03:16:11,140
And you'll be here In my arms

1375
03:16:11,140 --> 03:16:15,140
Just sleeping

1376
03:16:15,140 --> 03:16:20,560
What can you see

1377
03:16:20,560 --> 03:16:25,690
On the horizon?

1378
03:16:25,690 --> 03:16:30,660
Why do the white gulls

1379
03:16:30,660 --> 03:16:36,250
Call?

1380
03:16:36,250 --> 03:16:41,500
Across the sea

1381
03:16:41,500 --> 03:16:46,670
A pale moon rises

1382
03:16:46,670 --> 03:16:49,630
The ships have come

1383
03:16:49,630 --> 03:16:57,180
To carry you home

1384
03:16:57,180 --> 03:17:02,190
And all will turn

1385
03:17:02,190 --> 03:17:07,860
To silver glass

1386
03:17:07,860 --> 03:17:12,200
A light on the water

1387
03:17:12,200 --> 03:17:16,120
Grey ships pass

1388
03:17:16,120 --> 03:17:22,400
Into the West

